WEBVTT

00:00:23.223 --> 00:00:26.454
These should be familiar images
to everyone who remembers

00:00:26.526 --> 00:00:29.120
the USS Voyager's
triumphant return to Earth

00:00:29.195 --> 00:00:31.720
after 23 years
in the Delta Quadrant.

00:00:31.798 --> 00:00:34.289
Voyager captivated the hearts
and minds of the people

00:00:34.367 --> 00:00:36.631
throughout the Federation,
so it seems fitting

00:00:36.703 --> 00:00:39.137
that on this, the tenth
anniversary of their return,

00:00:39.205 --> 00:00:40.638
we take a moment to recall

00:00:40.707 --> 00:00:42.971
the sacrifices made
by the crew.

00:00:43.043 --> 00:00:44.908
Corruption charges
were brought today...

00:00:44.978 --> 00:00:47.003
Computer, end display.

00:02:50.703 --> 00:02:52.295
Hi! Good to see you.

00:02:52.372 --> 00:02:53.304
Dinner next week, then?

00:02:53.373 --> 00:02:56.501
Great. Okay.

00:02:58.711 --> 00:03:00.975
Hello.

00:03:01.047 --> 00:03:02.241
What's your name?

00:03:02.315 --> 00:03:03.907
Harry. What's yours?

00:03:03.983 --> 00:03:05.575
Sabrina.

00:03:05.652 --> 00:03:07.085
Naomi's daughter?

00:03:07.153 --> 00:03:09.417
- Uh-huh.
- You've gotten so big.

00:03:09.489 --> 00:03:11.218
I don't remember you.

00:03:11.291 --> 00:03:13.156
I haven't come
to one of these reunions

00:03:13.226 --> 00:03:14.158
in four years.

00:03:14.227 --> 00:03:15.159
Why?

00:03:15.228 --> 00:03:17.162
I've been
on a deep space assignment.

00:03:17.230 --> 00:03:19.130
For four years?

00:03:19.199 --> 00:03:21.793
Compared to how long
I was on Voyager,

00:03:21.868 --> 00:03:23.927
it seemed like a long weekend.

00:03:24.037 --> 00:03:25.937
Can you find your mother for me?

00:03:26.005 --> 00:03:27.302
- Uh-huh.
- I'd like to say hi.

00:03:28.675 --> 00:03:30.609
Oops. Here you are, Captain.

00:03:30.677 --> 00:03:32.042
Thank you, Admiral.

00:03:32.111 --> 00:03:34.739
I haven't seen her
since she was a baby.

00:03:34.814 --> 00:03:38.045
It's amazing how fast
you've all grown.

00:03:38.117 --> 00:03:39.778
How's Tuvok?

00:03:39.852 --> 00:03:40.910
Not well.

00:03:40.987 --> 00:03:43.785
I thought maybe I'd go
see him tomorrow.

00:03:43.856 --> 00:03:46.450
Oh, that would be nice.

00:03:46.526 --> 00:03:48.585
I'm sorry I missed the funeral.

00:03:48.661 --> 00:03:49.958
I should've been there.

00:03:50.029 --> 00:03:53.328
You were on a mission.
Everyone understood.

00:03:53.399 --> 00:03:55.765
It's so good to see you, Harry.

00:03:59.505 --> 00:04:00.767
Doc.

00:04:00.840 --> 00:04:02.102
Mr. Paris.

00:04:02.175 --> 00:04:03.904
Voyager's pilot, medic,

00:04:04.043 --> 00:04:06.637
and occasional thorn in my side.

00:04:06.713 --> 00:04:08.442
Where have you
been hiding yourself?

00:04:08.514 --> 00:04:09.776
I've been busy.

00:04:09.849 --> 00:04:10.781
New holonovel?

00:04:10.850 --> 00:04:12.579
I'll make sure to get your input

00:04:12.652 --> 00:04:14.711
before I send it off
to my publisher.

00:04:16.889 --> 00:04:18.823
Aren't you going
to introduce me to your date?

00:04:18.891 --> 00:04:23.260
Mr. Paris, meet Lana,
my blushing bride.

00:04:23.329 --> 00:04:24.353
You're married?

00:04:24.430 --> 00:04:27.092
Tomorrow is our
two-week anniversary.

00:04:27.166 --> 00:04:28.633
Well, congratulations.

00:04:28.701 --> 00:04:31.602
My invitation must've
gotten lost in subspace.

00:04:31.671 --> 00:04:32.933
Oh, you should be flattered.

00:04:33.006 --> 00:04:35.201
We took a page
from your book and eloped.

00:04:35.275 --> 00:04:37.709
Joe has a real flair
for romantic gestures.

00:04:37.777 --> 00:04:38.766
"Joe"?

00:04:38.845 --> 00:04:41.939
I decided I couldn't
get married without a name.

00:04:42.015 --> 00:04:46.349
It took you 33 years
to come up with Joe?

00:04:46.419 --> 00:04:48.614
It was Lana's
grandfather's name.

00:04:48.688 --> 00:04:52.419
Oh. Oh, so you're not a...

00:04:52.492 --> 00:04:54.460
A hologram? No.

00:04:54.527 --> 00:04:56.961
Frankly, Mr. Paris,
I'm surprised you'd even ask.

00:04:57.030 --> 00:04:58.725
I thought we were
beyond those sorts

00:04:58.798 --> 00:04:59.730
- of distinctions.
- Are you kidding?

00:04:59.799 --> 00:05:00.823
I think it's great.

00:05:00.900 --> 00:05:03.232
I'm in a mixed marriage
myself, remember?

00:05:03.303 --> 00:05:05.100
Speaking of which,
where is that wife of yours?

00:05:05.171 --> 00:05:07.298
The High Council had
a lot of questions.

00:05:07.373 --> 00:05:08.670
What did you tell them?

00:05:08.741 --> 00:05:12.905
The truth...
with a Klingon twist.

00:05:12.979 --> 00:05:15.709
I told them
that my beloved former Captain,

00:05:15.782 --> 00:05:17.249
who had saved my life many times

00:05:17.317 --> 00:05:19.785
in glorious battle,
would be honored

00:05:19.852 --> 00:05:22.116
to submit Korath's House
for consideration.

00:05:22.188 --> 00:05:23.382
Do you think it'll work?

00:05:23.456 --> 00:05:25.424
I'm just the Federation liaison,

00:05:25.491 --> 00:05:28.085
but I'd like to think
I have some influence.

00:05:29.562 --> 00:05:30.927
You still haven't told me

00:05:30.997 --> 00:05:32.931
why you're trying to help
Korath.

00:05:32.999 --> 00:05:34.933
He's an old friend.

00:05:35.001 --> 00:05:37.333
Would this old friend
have anything to do

00:05:37.403 --> 00:05:40.065
with the mission that
you sent my daughter on?

00:05:40.139 --> 00:05:41.071
Sorry, B'Elanna,

00:05:41.140 --> 00:05:43.267
but you know
I can't talk about that.

00:05:43.343 --> 00:05:45.106
Couldn't you at least have
waited until after the reunion?

00:05:45.178 --> 00:05:46.110
She really wanted to be here.

00:05:46.179 --> 00:05:48.113
She'll be home soon, I promise.

00:05:50.183 --> 00:05:52.777
May I have everyone's
attention, please?

00:05:56.923 --> 00:06:00.950
Ten years ago tonight,
this crew returned home

00:06:01.027 --> 00:06:04.258
from the longest away mission
in Starfleet history.

00:06:05.631 --> 00:06:08.998
23 years together
made you a family,

00:06:09.068 --> 00:06:12.265
one I'm proud
to have been adopted by.

00:06:12.338 --> 00:06:16.570
So let us raise our glasses...
to the journey.

00:06:16.642 --> 00:06:18.234
To the journey.

00:06:18.311 --> 00:06:21.769
And to those who aren't here
to celebrate it with us.

00:06:28.388 --> 00:06:32.256
Ladies and gentlemen,
meet the Borg.

00:06:32.325 --> 00:06:35.226
Over the course of this term,
you're going to become

00:06:35.294 --> 00:06:37.660
intimately familiar
with the collective.

00:06:37.730 --> 00:06:40.164
You'll learn
about the assimilation process,

00:06:40.233 --> 00:06:41.666
the Borg hierarchy,

00:06:41.734 --> 00:06:44.134
and the psychology
of the hive mind.

00:06:44.203 --> 00:06:47.195
And when it comes to your
performance in this class,

00:06:47.273 --> 00:06:50.140
my expectations are going
to be no different

00:06:50.209 --> 00:06:51.870
than the Borg Queen herself...
perfection.

00:06:53.179 --> 00:06:57.275
This semester,
we are very fortunate

00:06:57.350 --> 00:06:59.341
to have a special
guest lecturer,

00:06:59.419 --> 00:07:03.446
the woman who literally wrote
the book on the Borg...

00:07:03.523 --> 00:07:05.252
Admiral Kathryn Janeway.

00:07:06.592 --> 00:07:08.822
Thank you, Commander.

00:07:08.895 --> 00:07:10.886
I'm glad to be here.

00:07:10.997 --> 00:07:12.294
A question already, Cadet?

00:07:14.000 --> 00:07:16.491
I suppose it could wait
until after class, Admiral.

00:07:16.569 --> 00:07:19.231
As they say in the Temporal
Mechanics Department,

00:07:19.305 --> 00:07:20.966
"There's no time
like the present."

00:07:22.241 --> 00:07:24.232
In the year 2377, you aided

00:07:24.310 --> 00:07:27.040
the Borg resistance movement
known as Unimatrix Zero.

00:07:27.113 --> 00:07:28.910
Sounds like someone's been
reading ahead.

00:07:28.981 --> 00:07:31.575
I thought you had
a question, Cadet.

00:07:31.651 --> 00:07:32.913
Yes, ma'am.

00:07:32.985 --> 00:07:34.850
When you informed the Queen

00:07:34.921 --> 00:07:37.549
that you were going to liberate
thousands of her drones,

00:07:37.623 --> 00:07:40.148
could you describe
the look on her face?

00:07:42.094 --> 00:07:44.255
Admiral?

00:07:44.330 --> 00:07:46.594
Some of us were talking
before class,

00:07:46.666 --> 00:07:47.758
and we were curious.

00:07:47.834 --> 00:07:49.699
How extensive was
Seven of Nine's involvement

00:07:49.769 --> 00:07:51.760
with Unimatrix Zero?

00:07:52.839 --> 00:07:55.603
I'd, uh...

00:07:55.675 --> 00:07:58.143
prefer not to discuss
Seven of Nine.

00:07:58.211 --> 00:08:00.509
Yes, ma'am.

00:08:00.580 --> 00:08:03.572
Sorry.

00:08:08.354 --> 00:08:10.151
Excuse me.

00:08:14.794 --> 00:08:15.988
Okay.

00:08:16.062 --> 00:08:19.589
Uh, who can tell me
a little about nanotechnology?

00:08:21.934 --> 00:08:23.902
I'm sorry to pull you
out of class, Admiral.

00:08:23.970 --> 00:08:24.902
Did you see it?

00:08:24.971 --> 00:08:25.903
Yes, ma'am.

00:08:25.972 --> 00:08:26.904
And?

00:08:26.973 --> 00:08:28.463
It works.

00:08:29.876 --> 00:08:31.810
Korath has agreed
to the exchange?

00:08:31.878 --> 00:08:33.812
Yes.

00:08:33.880 --> 00:08:35.609
But...

00:08:35.681 --> 00:08:37.740
He's insisting on handing it
over to you personally.

00:08:40.186 --> 00:08:42.120
I'll be there as soon as I can.

00:08:42.188 --> 00:08:44.156
Good work, Ensign Paris.

00:09:04.610 --> 00:09:06.043
Hello, Tuvok.

00:09:06.112 --> 00:09:07.204
The light.

00:09:07.280 --> 00:09:08.907
Oh, I'm sorry.

00:09:17.123 --> 00:09:18.385
I know you.

00:09:18.457 --> 00:09:19.389
That's right.

00:09:19.458 --> 00:09:23.918
I'm your friend,
Kathryn Janeway, remember?

00:09:24.964 --> 00:09:26.556
You're an impostor.

00:09:26.632 --> 00:09:28.566
No, Tuvok. It's me.

00:09:28.634 --> 00:09:31.398
Admiral Janeway visits
on Sunday.

00:09:31.470 --> 00:09:32.903
Today is Thursday.

00:09:32.972 --> 00:09:36.931
Logic dictates that you are not
who you claim to be.

00:09:43.149 --> 00:09:44.912
How are you?

00:09:45.017 --> 00:09:46.917
I am close
to completing my work.

00:09:47.019 --> 00:09:48.543
I'm glad to hear it.

00:09:48.621 --> 00:09:52.318
It is difficult
with so many interruptions.

00:09:52.391 --> 00:09:53.483
I'm sorry.

00:09:53.559 --> 00:09:54.890
Would you like me to leave?

00:09:56.696 --> 00:09:58.664
You may stay.

00:10:03.402 --> 00:10:05.336
Tuvok?

00:10:07.373 --> 00:10:10.365
There's something I need
to tell you.

00:10:10.443 --> 00:10:12.411
It's very important.

00:10:22.521 --> 00:10:29.188
I'm going away,
and I may not see you again.

00:10:34.500 --> 00:10:37.901
Commander Barclay and the Doctor
will continue to visit.

00:10:37.970 --> 00:10:41.963
They'll bring you
anything you need.

00:10:42.041 --> 00:10:44.134
The Doctor comes on Wednesdays.

00:10:44.210 --> 00:10:48.476
Commander Barclay's
visits are...

00:10:48.547 --> 00:10:50.538
e-erratic.

00:11:20.880 --> 00:11:23.280
Good-bye, Tuvok.

00:11:46.539 --> 00:11:50.475
You must be the only doctor
who still makes house calls.

00:11:50.543 --> 00:11:51.635
What are your symptoms?

00:11:51.711 --> 00:11:53.474
I'm perfectly fine.

00:11:53.546 --> 00:11:55.309
For 33 years, you fought me

00:11:55.381 --> 00:11:57.144
every time you were due
for a physical.

00:11:57.216 --> 00:11:59.980
Now you ask me to give you one
ahead of schedule.

00:12:00.052 --> 00:12:00.984
I'm taking a trip.

00:12:01.053 --> 00:12:02.247
I just wanted
to get our appointment

00:12:02.321 --> 00:12:03.583
out of the way before I left.

00:12:03.656 --> 00:12:04.588
That's all?

00:12:04.657 --> 00:12:05.589
That's all.

00:12:05.658 --> 00:12:08.092
Hmm. The good news is

00:12:08.160 --> 00:12:10.458
you're as healthy as you were
the first day I examined you.

00:12:11.530 --> 00:12:12.656
Well...

00:12:12.732 --> 00:12:14.723
now that's out of the way,
have a seat.

00:12:14.800 --> 00:12:17.030
We didn't get to talk much
at the party.

00:12:17.103 --> 00:12:19.901
No. I don't suppose we did.

00:12:19.972 --> 00:12:21.906
So, how's married life?

00:12:21.974 --> 00:12:23.066
Wonderful.

00:12:23.142 --> 00:12:23.938
You should try it.

00:12:24.076 --> 00:12:26.271
Oh, I think it's a little late
for that.

00:12:26.345 --> 00:12:29.143
Marriage is for the young...
like your wife.

00:12:30.549 --> 00:12:33.643
I can only hope she ages
as gracefully as you have.

00:12:33.719 --> 00:12:35.914
I, of course, will be
the same handsome hologram

00:12:35.988 --> 00:12:37.888
20 years from now as I am today.

00:12:37.957 --> 00:12:40.187
I've been meaning to ask you...

00:12:40.259 --> 00:12:43.626
are you familiar with a
drug called chronexaline?

00:12:43.696 --> 00:12:45.425
We've been testing it
at Starfleet Medical

00:12:45.498 --> 00:12:47.125
to determine
if it can protect bio-matter

00:12:47.199 --> 00:12:48.666
from tachyon radiation.

00:12:48.734 --> 00:12:49.894
And?

00:12:49.969 --> 00:12:51.402
It's very promising.

00:12:51.470 --> 00:12:52.732
Why do you ask?

00:12:52.805 --> 00:12:56.332
I need 2,000 milligrams
by tomorrow afternoon.

00:12:58.377 --> 00:12:59.344
Why?

00:12:59.411 --> 00:13:01.140
That's classified.

00:13:01.213 --> 00:13:02.805
Will you get it for me?

00:13:06.485 --> 00:13:07.918
Of course, Admiral.

00:13:08.053 --> 00:13:09.452
You'll have it by 0900.

00:13:09.522 --> 00:13:10.648
Thank you.

00:13:16.929 --> 00:13:18.521
Download complete.

00:13:18.597 --> 00:13:21.395
This should be everything
you need.

00:13:22.935 --> 00:13:23.867
The shuttle?

00:13:23.936 --> 00:13:26.029
Waiting for you
at the Oakland shipyard.

00:13:26.105 --> 00:13:27.538
I wish you'd let me
come with you.

00:13:27.606 --> 00:13:30.200
Sorry, Reg,
but this is my mission.

00:13:30.276 --> 00:13:32.369
Besides, if you leave,
there won't be anyone

00:13:32.444 --> 00:13:35.208
to teach those eager
young cadets about the Borg.

00:13:35.281 --> 00:13:36.908
Oh.

00:13:39.618 --> 00:13:42.712
I made you some fresh tea
for the trip.

00:13:42.788 --> 00:13:44.380
Not that replicated stuff.

00:13:44.456 --> 00:13:46.549
Thank you...

00:13:46.625 --> 00:13:48.388
for everything.

00:13:48.460 --> 00:13:50.553
I wouldn't have been able
to do this without you.

00:13:50.629 --> 00:13:53.257
Oh, don't remind me.

00:14:01.307 --> 00:14:04.504
Any final words of advice
for your old Captain?

00:14:04.577 --> 00:14:07.842
Wait. Don't tell me.
I'm being impulsive.

00:14:07.913 --> 00:14:10.177
I haven't considered
all the consequences.

00:14:10.249 --> 00:14:12.080
It's too risky.

00:14:14.286 --> 00:14:16.277
Thanks for the input...

00:14:16.355 --> 00:14:19.847
but I've got to do
what I think is right.

00:14:22.361 --> 00:14:24.295
I know it wasn't easy
living all these years

00:14:24.363 --> 00:14:27.161
without her, Chakotay.

00:14:29.635 --> 00:14:31.694
But when I'm through,

00:14:31.770 --> 00:14:34.398
things might be better
for all of us.

00:14:38.844 --> 00:14:41.870
Trust me.

00:14:50.289 --> 00:14:52.223
Tom?

00:14:54.627 --> 00:14:56.492
Tom.

00:14:56.562 --> 00:14:57.824
I'm sleeping.

00:14:57.897 --> 00:14:59.489
It's time.

00:14:59.565 --> 00:15:01.829
For what?

00:15:01.901 --> 00:15:04.301
I'll give you one guess.

00:15:09.909 --> 00:15:11.376
Paris to...

00:15:13.913 --> 00:15:15.676
Paris to Sick Bay. It's time.

00:15:15.748 --> 00:15:17.716
Remain calm, Mr. Paris.

00:15:17.783 --> 00:15:20.343
Can she stand?

00:15:20.419 --> 00:15:22.011
Affirmative.

00:15:22.087 --> 00:15:24.578
Then I suggest
you report to Sick Bay.

00:15:27.426 --> 00:15:28.859
What about B'Elanna?

00:15:28.928 --> 00:15:29.895
Her, too.

00:15:29.962 --> 00:15:31.554
Right, of course.

00:15:31.630 --> 00:15:33.564
Maybe we should take
the transporter.

00:15:33.632 --> 00:15:36.829
Hey, wait for me!

00:15:41.106 --> 00:15:43.074
Hmm...

00:15:43.142 --> 00:15:44.700
What do you mean by "hmm"?

00:15:44.777 --> 00:15:48.372
You're going to have
a very healthy baby...

00:15:48.447 --> 00:15:50.039
but not tonight.

00:15:50.115 --> 00:15:51.514
Tell me you're joking.

00:15:51.583 --> 00:15:54.177
You're experiencing
false labor, Lieutenant.

00:15:54.253 --> 00:15:55.845
- Again?
- As I explained

00:15:55.921 --> 00:15:57.582
the last time,
it's a common occurrence,

00:15:57.656 --> 00:15:59.248
especially among Klingons.

00:15:59.325 --> 00:16:02.590
I want this thing out of me
now!

00:16:02.661 --> 00:16:03.889
Misdirected rage...

00:16:03.996 --> 00:16:05.987
another common occurrence
among Klingons.

00:16:06.065 --> 00:16:07.327
Can't you induce?

00:16:07.399 --> 00:16:08.832
I wouldn't recommend it.

00:16:08.901 --> 00:16:11.461
If this keeps happening,
we'll never get any sleep.

00:16:11.537 --> 00:16:13.596
You think it's bad now?

00:16:13.672 --> 00:16:14.696
When?

00:16:14.773 --> 00:16:15.831
0400.

00:16:15.908 --> 00:16:17.500
How many false alarms
does that make?

00:16:17.576 --> 00:16:18.907
Three that we know of.

00:16:18.978 --> 00:16:20.707
That baby is as
stubborn as her mother.

00:16:20.779 --> 00:16:23.373
Harry's starting a pool to see
who can guess the actual date

00:16:23.449 --> 00:16:25.849
and time of birth.

00:16:25.918 --> 00:16:29.012
Tell him to put me down
for next... Friday,

00:16:29.088 --> 00:16:31.022
2300 hours.

00:16:31.090 --> 00:16:32.216
Anything else?

00:16:32.291 --> 00:16:33.883
Crewman Chell's asked

00:16:33.959 --> 00:16:36.154
about taking over
in the Mess Hall full-time.

00:16:36.228 --> 00:16:38.753
Neelix left some pretty
big pots and pans to fill.

00:16:38.831 --> 00:16:42.028
Does Mr. Chell feel
he's up to the challenge?

00:16:42.101 --> 00:16:43.534
Apparently so.

00:16:43.602 --> 00:16:45.160
He's prepared a sample menu.

00:16:46.772 --> 00:16:49.036
"Plasma Leak Soup,

00:16:49.108 --> 00:16:52.475
Chicken Warp Core-don Bleu."

00:16:54.213 --> 00:16:57.410
If his cooking's as bad
as his puns, we're in trouble.

00:16:57.483 --> 00:16:58.848
Oh, I don't know...
I wouldn't mind giving

00:16:58.917 --> 00:17:00.578
his "Red Alert Chili" a try.

00:17:00.652 --> 00:17:01.710
Feel like having lunch?

00:17:01.787 --> 00:17:03.880
I'd love to,
but I've already made plans.

00:17:03.956 --> 00:17:05.218
Rain check?

00:17:05.290 --> 00:17:06.188
Absolutely.

00:17:17.870 --> 00:17:19.895
What's all this?

00:17:20.039 --> 00:17:21.301
A picnic.

00:17:21.373 --> 00:17:23.068
According to my research,

00:17:23.142 --> 00:17:25.804
this is an appropriate
third date.

00:17:27.813 --> 00:17:30.213
You didn't have to go
to this much trouble.

00:17:30.282 --> 00:17:31.874
If this makes you uncomfortable,

00:17:31.950 --> 00:17:33.542
I could prepare
a less elaborate meal.

00:17:33.619 --> 00:17:38.386
No, don't change a thing.

00:17:38.457 --> 00:17:40.948
This is perfection.

00:17:59.845 --> 00:18:03.474
In the interest of fair play,
I should inform you

00:18:03.549 --> 00:18:06.609
that Mr. Kim has never
defeated me at kal-toh.

00:18:12.391 --> 00:18:13.949
You should've listened to me.

00:18:20.065 --> 00:18:24.331
Kal-toh is as much a game
of patience as it is of logic.

00:18:24.403 --> 00:18:25.700
An experienced player

00:18:25.771 --> 00:18:26.999
will sometimes
take several hours

00:18:27.072 --> 00:18:30.007
to decide his next move,
and in some cases

00:18:30.075 --> 00:18:32.771
even days may be necessary to...

00:18:32.845 --> 00:18:34.005
Kal-toh.

00:18:34.079 --> 00:18:35.603
You beat him.

00:18:36.682 --> 00:18:39.276
Congratulations.

00:18:39.351 --> 00:18:41.911
I'm sure it was
just beginner's luck, sir.

00:18:42.020 --> 00:18:45.046
I'd offer you a rematch,
but I'm due in Astrometrics.

00:18:45.124 --> 00:18:47.388
Another time, perhaps.

00:18:52.030 --> 00:18:56.364
He may have to go,
but I'm free and feeling lucky.

00:18:56.435 --> 00:18:58.960
If you'll excuse me, Ensign.

00:19:01.073 --> 00:19:04.474
It's just a game, Tuvok.

00:19:04.543 --> 00:19:06.738
Icheb's an exceptionally
bright young man.

00:19:06.812 --> 00:19:07.801
Did it occur to you

00:19:07.880 --> 00:19:10.007
that he might simply be
a better player?

00:19:10.082 --> 00:19:11.879
My loss was the result

00:19:11.950 --> 00:19:14.680
of another lapse
in concentration.

00:19:14.753 --> 00:19:18.018
I am detecting
lower neuropeptide levels.

00:19:18.090 --> 00:19:19.682
As I suspected.

00:19:19.758 --> 00:19:22.522
My condition is deteriorating.

00:19:22.594 --> 00:19:25.188
It's a minor change.

00:19:25.264 --> 00:19:27.698
We knew it would happen.

00:19:27.766 --> 00:19:31.099
I simply have
to increase your medication.

00:19:34.273 --> 00:19:36.036
Thank you, Doctor.

00:19:36.108 --> 00:19:41.410
Commander... I understand
your desire for privacy,

00:19:41.480 --> 00:19:44.574
but maybe it's time
we informed the Captain.

00:19:44.650 --> 00:19:47.744
I will inform her
if and when the disorder

00:19:47.819 --> 00:19:50.413
begins to affect the
performance of my duties.

00:19:50.489 --> 00:19:53.083
Of course.

00:19:55.160 --> 00:19:55.260
Your move.

00:19:55.260 --> 00:19:56.386
Your move.

00:19:56.461 --> 00:19:59.453
Green... grid 1210.

00:20:02.534 --> 00:20:06.470
Red, grid 313.

00:20:06.538 --> 00:20:07.470
Tricky.

00:20:08.540 --> 00:20:09.529
How's Brax?

00:20:09.608 --> 00:20:10.540
Wonderful.

00:20:10.609 --> 00:20:12.600
Thanks for asking.

00:20:12.678 --> 00:20:14.612
I know I can never replace
his father, but...

00:20:14.680 --> 00:20:17.808
I have no doubt
the boy looks up to you.

00:20:18.884 --> 00:20:23.412
Orange, grid 1012.

00:20:23.488 --> 00:20:25.285
I haven't told anyone,

00:20:25.357 --> 00:20:28.554
but I'm thinking of asking Dexa
to marry me.

00:20:28.627 --> 00:20:30.458
She'd be wise to accept.

00:20:30.529 --> 00:20:34.397
That's enough of my love life.
How about yours?

00:20:34.466 --> 00:20:36.593
I don't have a love life.

00:20:36.668 --> 00:20:40.434
Oh? What about your relationship
with Commander Chakotay?

00:20:40.505 --> 00:20:42.302
It's your turn.

00:20:42.374 --> 00:20:44.638
Actually, it's yours.

00:20:44.710 --> 00:20:47.076
At least tell me
how he liked the picnic.

00:20:48.547 --> 00:20:52.142
It was an enjoyable activity
for both of us.

00:20:52.217 --> 00:20:53.844
Thank you for suggesting it.

00:20:53.919 --> 00:20:55.386
Anytime.

00:20:59.057 --> 00:21:00.991
What is it?

00:21:01.059 --> 00:21:02.754
Long-range sensors are detecting

00:21:02.828 --> 00:21:04.762
extremely high
neutrino emissions

00:21:04.830 --> 00:21:07.663
accompanied by
intermittent graviton flux

00:21:07.733 --> 00:21:10.600
approximately
three light-years away.

00:21:10.669 --> 00:21:12.398
A wormhole?

00:21:12.471 --> 00:21:14.462
I'm not sure.

00:21:14.539 --> 00:21:16.131
I'll need to conduct more scans.

00:21:16.208 --> 00:21:17.470
We can finish our game tomorrow.

00:21:17.542 --> 00:21:19.601
I'll contact you
at the usual time.

00:21:22.948 --> 00:21:25.314
The emissions are occurring
at the center of the nebula.

00:21:25.384 --> 00:21:27.409
There appear to be hundreds
of distinct sources.

00:21:27.486 --> 00:21:30.284
Which could translate
to hundreds of wormholes.

00:21:30.355 --> 00:21:32.949
The radiation is interfering
with our sensors,

00:21:33.025 --> 00:21:35.289
but if Ensign Kim's
enthusiasm turns out

00:21:35.360 --> 00:21:38.295
to be justified, it would be
the most concentrated occurrence

00:21:38.363 --> 00:21:39.796
of wormholes ever recorded.

00:21:39.865 --> 00:21:41.127
Any idea where they lead?

00:21:41.199 --> 00:21:42.461
Not yet, but if just

00:21:42.534 --> 00:21:44.161
one of them leads
to the Alpha Quadrant...

00:21:44.236 --> 00:21:45.498
Who knows, Harry?

00:21:45.570 --> 00:21:48.596
It might take us right into
your parents' living room.

00:21:48.674 --> 00:21:51.108
Alter course, Mr. Paris.

00:21:51.176 --> 00:21:53.269
Ensign, when you speak
to your mother,

00:21:53.345 --> 00:21:55.813
tell her we may need her
to move the sofa.

00:22:01.753 --> 00:22:04.586
7153... 5331...

00:22:04.656 --> 00:22:07.420
7153... 5331...

00:22:07.492 --> 00:22:09.585
- 7153...
- I'm sorry if I pulled you away

00:22:09.661 --> 00:22:10.650
from something important, sir,

00:22:10.729 --> 00:22:11.855
but he won't let
anyone near him,

00:22:11.930 --> 00:22:13.761
- and I thought you might...
- You did the right thing.

00:22:13.832 --> 00:22:15.493
His condition's
never been associated

00:22:15.567 --> 00:22:16.591
with violent behavior.

00:22:16.668 --> 00:22:18.260
He seems more frustrated
than violent.

00:22:18.337 --> 00:22:20.771
Long-range sensors
have detected no trace.

00:22:20.839 --> 00:22:22.602
Her disappearance
remains a mystery.

00:22:22.674 --> 00:22:24.107
I am deeply concerned.

00:22:24.176 --> 00:22:25.939
What are you concerned
about, Tuvok?

00:22:26.011 --> 00:22:26.943
Her disappearance.

00:22:27.012 --> 00:22:28.445
- Whose?
- 5331...

00:22:28.513 --> 00:22:30.447
7153.

00:22:30.515 --> 00:22:32.107
He's been repeating
those same numbers

00:22:32.184 --> 00:22:34.778
over and over again...
533171.

00:22:34.853 --> 00:22:36.115
It might be a stardate.

00:22:36.188 --> 00:22:39.453
Stardate 53317...

00:22:39.524 --> 00:22:40.957
If my memory files are accurate,

00:22:41.026 --> 00:22:43.620
that was the day Captain Janeway
was abducted by the Kellidians.

00:22:43.695 --> 00:22:45.959
Is that who you're talking
about, Tuvok, Captain Janeway?

00:22:46.031 --> 00:22:47.464
Her disappearance remains
a mystery.

00:22:47.532 --> 00:22:49.466
No, you solved
that mystery, Tuvok.

00:22:49.534 --> 00:22:51.297
You rescued the Captain
and brought her

00:22:51.370 --> 00:22:53.463
back to Voyager
safe and sound, remember?

00:22:53.538 --> 00:22:55.802
I am deeply concerned,
deeply concerned.

00:22:55.874 --> 00:22:57.808
Maybe if the Admiral
paid him a visit,

00:22:57.876 --> 00:22:59.138
showed him
that she was all right?

00:22:59.211 --> 00:23:00.974
Unfortunately, she's
out of town right now.

00:23:01.046 --> 00:23:02.411
I'm not sure
when she'll be back.

00:23:02.481 --> 00:23:05.075
She's never coming back!

00:23:05.150 --> 00:23:07.414
Her disappearance
remains a mystery.

00:23:07.486 --> 00:23:10.922
I'm deeply concerned...

00:23:15.660 --> 00:23:17.924
Voyager to Pathfinder.

00:23:18.029 --> 00:23:19.724
Come in, Pathfinder.

00:23:19.798 --> 00:23:21.231
Doctor, what a pleasant sur...

00:23:21.299 --> 00:23:23.460
Oh! I've forgotten about our
golf game again, haven't I?

00:23:23.535 --> 00:23:25.730
Relax, Reg,
it's not until next week.

00:23:25.804 --> 00:23:28.796
I'm here because I need to get
in touch with Admiral Janeway.

00:23:28.874 --> 00:23:30.808
Oh, she's out of town.

00:23:30.876 --> 00:23:33.743
I know. Did she tell you
where she was going?

00:23:33.812 --> 00:23:36.178
Uh, I'm afraid
it-it never came up.

00:23:36.248 --> 00:23:37.909
I mean, is something wrong?

00:23:37.983 --> 00:23:39.416
I'm not sure.

00:23:39.484 --> 00:23:41.611
I paid a visit to Tuvok
this morning.

00:23:41.686 --> 00:23:44.814
He seemed to think that she
was in some sort of danger.

00:23:44.890 --> 00:23:45.948
Well, you know
better than anyone

00:23:46.024 --> 00:23:48.458
how confused Tuvok can get.

00:23:48.527 --> 00:23:51.655
Yes, but I've been worried
about the Admiral, too.

00:23:51.730 --> 00:23:52.822
Why?

00:23:52.898 --> 00:23:54.160
Two days ago, she asked me

00:23:54.232 --> 00:23:57.531
for a large quantity
of an experimental medication.

00:23:57.602 --> 00:23:59.467
When I asked her
why she needed it,

00:23:59.538 --> 00:24:00.971
she said it was classified.

00:24:01.106 --> 00:24:03.506
Then you shouldn't be telling me
about it, should you?

00:24:03.575 --> 00:24:06.305
I spoke to Director Okaro
at Starfleet Intelligence.

00:24:06.378 --> 00:24:07.902
He assured me that the Admiral

00:24:07.979 --> 00:24:10.209
hasn't been involved
in any classified work

00:24:10.282 --> 00:24:12.375
since she began teaching
at the Academy.

00:24:12.451 --> 00:24:13.850
You know how sneaky

00:24:13.919 --> 00:24:15.386
these intelligence people
can be.

00:24:15.454 --> 00:24:17.217
Maybe he was just trying
to throw you off.

00:24:17.289 --> 00:24:18.483
Maybe...

00:24:18.557 --> 00:24:20.252
but still...

00:24:20.325 --> 00:24:21.917
she's been talking for months

00:24:21.993 --> 00:24:24.655
about how excited she is
to be teaching with you.

00:24:24.729 --> 00:24:27.721
Then,
just as the semester begins,

00:24:27.799 --> 00:24:31.929
she goes away...
without even telling you where.

00:24:32.003 --> 00:24:35.404
Don't you find that
a little strange?

00:24:35.474 --> 00:24:40.036
I... I'm sure that there
is a perfectly reasonable

00:24:40.111 --> 00:24:41.840
explanation, Doctor.

00:24:41.913 --> 00:24:43.403
I'm sorry,

00:24:43.482 --> 00:24:47.543
I have some... papers to grade.

00:24:47.619 --> 00:24:49.314
You're stammering, Reg.

00:24:49.387 --> 00:24:50.649
So?!

00:24:52.324 --> 00:24:55.452
I haven't heard you do that
in years.

00:24:55.527 --> 00:24:57.791
I think you do know
where she is.

00:24:57.863 --> 00:24:59.490
She is one of the most
decorated officers

00:24:59.564 --> 00:25:01.122
in all of Starfleet history.

00:25:01.199 --> 00:25:04.396
I'm... I'm...

00:25:04.469 --> 00:25:06.528
sure she can
take care of herself.

00:25:06.605 --> 00:25:07.731
You wouldn't be saying that

00:25:07.806 --> 00:25:09.831
unless she was doing
something dangerous.

00:25:09.908 --> 00:25:11.603
You are putting words
in my mouth.

00:25:11.676 --> 00:25:14.440
Tell me where she is, Reg.

00:25:32.631 --> 00:25:35.065
Welcome to the House
of Korath, Admiral.

00:25:35.133 --> 00:25:37.101
I love what he's
done with the place.

00:25:45.644 --> 00:25:47.407
What was that about?

00:25:47.479 --> 00:25:49.913
He said your demeanor
was disrespectful.

00:25:49.981 --> 00:25:52.916
I hope you told him
I didn't mean to be rude.

00:25:52.984 --> 00:25:53.916
I told him if he didn't

00:25:53.985 --> 00:25:56.783
show you more respect,
I would break his arm.

00:25:56.855 --> 00:25:58.652
You are your mother's daughter.

00:25:59.724 --> 00:26:01.954
Korath is waiting.
We should go in.

00:26:02.027 --> 00:26:04.154
Sorry, but this is
where we part ways.

00:26:04.229 --> 00:26:05.491
Excuse me?

00:26:05.564 --> 00:26:07.088
You're dismissed, Ensign.

00:26:07.165 --> 00:26:09.258
Admiral, I really think that...

00:26:09.334 --> 00:26:10.892
I can take care of myself.

00:26:11.036 --> 00:26:12.503
With all due respect,

00:26:12.571 --> 00:26:14.596
I've been working on this
for six months, and...

00:26:14.673 --> 00:26:17.073
And you've done
an exemplary job, but it's over.

00:26:17.142 --> 00:26:18.905
Understood?

00:26:18.977 --> 00:26:21.912
Yes, ma'am.

00:26:22.013 --> 00:26:23.446
I happen to know

00:26:23.515 --> 00:26:25.813
your parents are anxious
to spend some time with you.

00:26:25.884 --> 00:26:27.317
Take a few days' leave.

00:26:27.385 --> 00:26:29.876
Go and see them.

00:26:50.642 --> 00:26:53.577
A Cardassian disruptor.

00:26:53.645 --> 00:26:57.308
I've modified it
to emit a nadion pulse.

00:26:57.382 --> 00:27:01.512
Impressive, but that's not
what I've come for.

00:27:03.455 --> 00:27:04.786
No.

00:27:04.856 --> 00:27:09.350
You've come for something
far more dangerous.

00:27:09.427 --> 00:27:11.861
Where is it?

00:27:11.930 --> 00:27:13.898
Somewhere safe.

00:27:15.934 --> 00:27:17.902
I went to a great deal
of trouble

00:27:17.969 --> 00:27:20.233
to get you your seat
on the High Council.

00:27:20.305 --> 00:27:22.705
Now give me what you promised.

00:27:34.119 --> 00:27:36.053
I've scanned your shuttle.

00:27:36.121 --> 00:27:39.056
It appears you've made some...

00:27:39.124 --> 00:27:44.221
interesting modifications.

00:27:44.295 --> 00:27:48.425
Your shields generator
is of particular interest.

00:27:48.500 --> 00:27:50.058
It's not for sale.

00:27:52.971 --> 00:27:56.737
Then what you want
isn't available, either.

00:27:58.910 --> 00:28:01.504
We had an agreement.

00:28:01.579 --> 00:28:04.104
Show the Admiral out.

00:28:18.129 --> 00:28:21.496
Maybe Chell should add
"Nebula Soup" to his menu.

00:28:22.734 --> 00:28:23.826
Shields.

00:28:23.902 --> 00:28:24.834
Holding.

00:28:24.903 --> 00:28:26.063
Bridge to Astrometrics.

00:28:26.137 --> 00:28:27.069
Go ahead.

00:28:27.138 --> 00:28:29.333
Any more data on those
neutrino emissions?

00:28:29.407 --> 00:28:31.841
Negative, Captain.
I still can't get a clear scan.

00:28:31.910 --> 00:28:33.673
Distance to the center?

00:28:33.745 --> 00:28:35.713
Six million kilometers.

00:28:36.948 --> 00:28:38.040
What is it?

00:28:38.116 --> 00:28:39.583
I'm detecting

00:28:39.651 --> 00:28:43.348
a tritanium signature,
bearing 342 mark 55.

00:28:43.421 --> 00:28:45.389
Whatever it is, it's too close.

00:28:45.457 --> 00:28:46.890
Evasive maneuvers.

00:28:48.993 --> 00:28:51.188
Was it a ship?

00:28:51.262 --> 00:28:52.854
Possibly.

00:28:56.301 --> 00:28:59.566
Another tritanium signature
right on top of us.

00:29:03.675 --> 00:29:04.937
Tom!

00:29:12.283 --> 00:29:14.911
Get us out of here now.

00:29:16.721 --> 00:29:21.215
Vessel identified: USS Voyager.

00:29:21.292 --> 00:29:23.726
We will pursue and assimilate.

00:29:23.795 --> 00:29:27.561
No, they haven't compromised
our security.

00:29:27.632 --> 00:29:31.932
Let the vessel continue...
for now.

00:29:33.471 --> 00:29:36.440
I'll keep an eye on them.

00:29:42.814 --> 00:29:45.749
There's no evidence
that the cube detected us.

00:29:45.817 --> 00:29:46.909
Where is it now?

00:29:46.985 --> 00:29:48.748
Approximately
three light-years away.

00:29:48.820 --> 00:29:50.082
How could they not have seen us?

00:29:50.155 --> 00:29:52.419
We came within ten meters
of their hull.

00:29:52.490 --> 00:29:54.253
The Borg wouldn't
knowingly risk a collision.

00:29:54.325 --> 00:29:56.919
The radiation must've interfered
with their sensors as well.

00:29:56.995 --> 00:29:59.088
If they can't detect
us, we should go back.

00:29:59.164 --> 00:30:00.426
I wouldn't recommend it.

00:30:00.498 --> 00:30:02.261
My analysis
of the tritanium signature

00:30:02.333 --> 00:30:04.597
suggests there were
at least 47 Borg vessels

00:30:04.669 --> 00:30:05.761
inside the nebula.

00:30:05.837 --> 00:30:07.771
We can't just give up
on those wormholes.

00:30:07.839 --> 00:30:08.771
Oh, yes, we can.

00:30:08.840 --> 00:30:10.273
What if we try to modify?

00:30:10.341 --> 00:30:11.603
Sorry, Mr. Kim.

00:30:11.676 --> 00:30:16.010
You may be the Captain someday,
but not today.

00:30:25.857 --> 00:30:27.950
Tom.

00:30:28.026 --> 00:30:29.459
What are you doing
when your shift ends?

00:30:29.527 --> 00:30:30.789
Uh, no plans. Why?

00:30:30.862 --> 00:30:32.454
Uh, I've been thinking.

00:30:32.530 --> 00:30:34.464
You and I should have some fun.

00:30:34.532 --> 00:30:35.624
One last adventure

00:30:35.700 --> 00:30:37.292
before you get too busy
being a father.

00:30:37.368 --> 00:30:39.131
Did you reserve
some holodeck time?

00:30:39.204 --> 00:30:41.331
I got a better idea.

00:30:42.373 --> 00:30:44.933
This is your idea of fun?

00:30:45.009 --> 00:30:46.476
Lt'll work;
we just need to make

00:30:46.544 --> 00:30:48.205
a few modifications
to the Flyer.

00:30:48.279 --> 00:30:50.747
We might as well just
hand it over to the Borg.

00:30:50.815 --> 00:30:51.839
How could that happen

00:30:51.916 --> 00:30:55.511
with the best pilot
in the Quadrant at the helm?

00:30:55.587 --> 00:30:56.986
Nice try.

00:30:57.121 --> 00:30:58.554
If we go to the Captain
together,

00:30:58.623 --> 00:31:00.989
she'll be much more likely
to approve my plan.

00:31:01.059 --> 00:31:02.390
I don't want her to approve it.

00:31:02.460 --> 00:31:03.893
Where's your sense of adventure?

00:31:03.962 --> 00:31:05.259
I left it in that nebula,

00:31:05.330 --> 00:31:07.025
and I'm not going back for it.

00:31:07.098 --> 00:31:09.066
Don't you want
to find a way home?

00:31:09.133 --> 00:31:10.600
I am home, Harry.

00:31:16.107 --> 00:31:20.100
Captain Proton would never walk
away from a mission like this.

00:31:20.178 --> 00:31:21.440
Captain Proton
doesn't have a wife

00:31:21.512 --> 00:31:23.980
and a baby on the way.

00:31:28.353 --> 00:31:30.116
If you're here
for my daily report,

00:31:30.188 --> 00:31:31.621
it's not complete.

00:31:31.689 --> 00:31:33.623
Actually...

00:31:33.691 --> 00:31:36.785
I'm here
in an unofficial capacity.

00:31:36.861 --> 00:31:40.661
I was wondering if you'd
like to get together again.

00:31:42.533 --> 00:31:45.001
To do what?

00:31:46.204 --> 00:31:48.798
Well, that all depends
on your research.

00:31:48.873 --> 00:31:53.469
Would a quiet dinner
be an appropriate fourth date?

00:31:53.544 --> 00:31:57.674
Hmm, I believe it would be
a more suitable fifth date.

00:31:58.716 --> 00:32:02.447
I'm willing to skip
ahead if you are.

00:32:04.389 --> 00:32:08.553
You're fine, aside from
some minor inflammation

00:32:08.626 --> 00:32:10.890
around your biradial clamp.

00:32:10.962 --> 00:32:13.430
Let me know if it starts
to bother you.

00:32:16.467 --> 00:32:18.401
Is there something else?

00:32:18.469 --> 00:32:19.936
Do you remember
three months ago,

00:32:20.004 --> 00:32:22.199
when my cortical node shut down?

00:32:22.273 --> 00:32:23.604
How could I forget?

00:32:23.675 --> 00:32:26.109
You said it might be possible

00:32:26.177 --> 00:32:29.112
to remove the fail-safe device
that was causing the problem.

00:32:29.180 --> 00:32:30.875
Has it been giving you
trouble again?

00:32:30.949 --> 00:32:32.041
No,

00:32:32.116 --> 00:32:34.641
but I've reconsidered your offer
to extract it.

00:32:34.719 --> 00:32:37.051
I've been hoping you would.

00:32:37.121 --> 00:32:39.453
You said it would require
several surgeries.

00:32:39.524 --> 00:32:40.718
Actually,

00:32:40.792 --> 00:32:42.919
in anticipation of
your change of heart,

00:32:42.994 --> 00:32:45.394
I've been studying the problem
in more detail.

00:32:45.463 --> 00:32:47.294
I now believe I can reconfigure

00:32:47.365 --> 00:32:49.424
the microcircuitry
with a single procedure.

00:32:49.500 --> 00:32:52.958
You'll be free to experience
the full range of emotions...

00:32:53.037 --> 00:32:54.470
everything
from a hearty belly laugh

00:32:54.539 --> 00:32:56.530
to a good cry.

00:32:56.607 --> 00:32:57.869
How soon can you do it?

00:32:57.942 --> 00:32:59.967
Today, if you'd like.

00:33:00.111 --> 00:33:02.045
My shift ends at 1800 hours.

00:33:02.113 --> 00:33:04.081
It's a date.

00:33:05.616 --> 00:33:07.641
Speaking of dates...

00:33:07.719 --> 00:33:10.153
once the fail-safe is gone,

00:33:10.221 --> 00:33:14.055
you'll be free to pursue
more intimate relationships.

00:33:14.125 --> 00:33:15.217
I'm aware of that.

00:33:15.293 --> 00:33:16.555
If you decide you need help

00:33:16.627 --> 00:33:19.721
with that aspect
of your humanity...

00:33:19.797 --> 00:33:22.630
I'm always at your disposal.

00:33:23.968 --> 00:33:25.560
I appreciate that.

00:33:25.636 --> 00:33:27.069
Really?

00:33:27.138 --> 00:33:28.696
Yes...

00:33:28.773 --> 00:33:31.867
but I already have
all the help I need.

00:33:33.144 --> 00:33:34.236
Ah...

00:33:34.312 --> 00:33:37.247
of course.

00:33:37.315 --> 00:33:38.942
You'll undoubtedly be running

00:33:39.083 --> 00:33:41.745
more simulations
with the Chakotay hologram.

00:33:41.819 --> 00:33:44.253
No, actually.

00:33:44.322 --> 00:33:46.790
I'll see you at 1800 hours.

00:33:54.432 --> 00:33:58.129
Mak-taH hoon...
Janeway, ghuy'cha.

00:34:07.111 --> 00:34:08.908
I've reconsidered your offer.

00:34:09.047 --> 00:34:10.480
I thought you might.

00:34:10.548 --> 00:34:12.413
I'll give you
the shield emitter,

00:34:12.483 --> 00:34:16.385
but not until I've inspected
the device you're offering...

00:34:16.454 --> 00:34:18.422
to make sure it's genuine.

00:34:18.489 --> 00:34:20.548
You question my honor?!

00:34:20.625 --> 00:34:22.024
If you were honorable,

00:34:22.093 --> 00:34:25.790
you wouldn't have changed
the terms of our agreement.

00:34:29.200 --> 00:34:32.226
Show it to me, or I'm leaving.

00:34:55.893 --> 00:34:59.329
This will do just fine.

00:35:01.099 --> 00:35:02.361
Stop her!

00:35:07.505 --> 00:35:10.167
Computer, deploy armor.

00:35:14.212 --> 00:35:17.238
Lay in a course
for these coordinates.

00:35:27.925 --> 00:35:29.153
What do you want?

00:35:29.227 --> 00:35:31.718
You'll pay
for your deceit, ghuy'cha!

00:35:31.796 --> 00:35:33.423
And the house of Korath
won't rest

00:35:33.498 --> 00:35:36.831
until you've drowned
in your own blood!

00:35:36.901 --> 00:35:40.393
I'd love to stay and chat,
but I'm on a tight schedule.

00:35:40.471 --> 00:35:42.371
Computer, warp 6.

00:35:48.479 --> 00:35:50.777
Approaching
designated coordinates.

00:35:50.848 --> 00:35:52.110
All stop.

00:35:52.183 --> 00:35:56.483
Warning. Vessel approaching,
vector 121 mark six.

00:36:04.428 --> 00:36:05.861
Harry.

00:36:05.930 --> 00:36:08.398
And people are always saying
that space is so big.

00:36:08.466 --> 00:36:10.229
Lower your shields, Admiral.

00:36:10.301 --> 00:36:11.700
Prepare for transport.

00:36:11.769 --> 00:36:13.396
I'm taking you into custody.

00:36:13.471 --> 00:36:16.497
You have no grounds
to take me into custody,

00:36:16.574 --> 00:36:17.836
Captain.

00:36:17.909 --> 00:36:21.208
Reg told the Doctor everything,
and the Doctor told me.

00:36:21.279 --> 00:36:25.375
Now, please, Admiral,
stand down.

00:36:25.449 --> 00:36:27.713
On one condition...

00:36:27.785 --> 00:36:30.549
you let me explain
why I'm doing this.

00:36:30.621 --> 00:36:32.885
You have no idea
what the consequences would be.

00:36:32.957 --> 00:36:35.721
I know what the consequences
are if we do nothing.

00:36:35.793 --> 00:36:37.192
So do you.

00:36:37.261 --> 00:36:40.594
I have a chance
to change all that.

00:36:42.300 --> 00:36:44.894
If Starfleet Command knew
what you were trying to do...

00:36:44.969 --> 00:36:46.231
You haven't told them?

00:36:46.304 --> 00:36:49.432
The Doctor and I decided
to keep things in the family.

00:36:49.507 --> 00:36:51.372
What about your crew?

00:36:51.442 --> 00:36:53.933
I told them I needed to take you
back to Starfleet Medical

00:36:54.045 --> 00:36:56.377
because you'd contracted
a rare disease.

00:36:56.447 --> 00:36:58.347
I hope it isn't terminal.

00:36:58.416 --> 00:36:59.610
No...

00:36:59.684 --> 00:37:01.618
but it has been known
to affect judgment.

00:37:01.686 --> 00:37:03.017
I know what I'm doing, Harry.

00:37:03.087 --> 00:37:04.554
Do you?

00:37:04.622 --> 00:37:07.352
Can you say with absolute
certainty that it'll work?

00:37:07.425 --> 00:37:09.518
Because if you can't...

00:37:09.594 --> 00:37:12.222
Even if it weren't a violation
of every rule in the book,

00:37:12.296 --> 00:37:14.264
it would still be far too risky.

00:37:15.566 --> 00:37:17.329
What?

00:37:17.401 --> 00:37:19.665
I'm remembering a young Ensign

00:37:19.737 --> 00:37:22.604
who wanted to fly
into a Borg-infested

00:37:22.673 --> 00:37:25.335
nebula, just to explore
the remote possibility

00:37:25.409 --> 00:37:27.604
that we might find a way home.

00:37:27.678 --> 00:37:31.136
If I remember correctly,
you stopped me.

00:37:31.215 --> 00:37:33.775
We didn't know then
what we know now.

00:37:35.152 --> 00:37:37.177
Our technology
may have advanced, but...

00:37:37.255 --> 00:37:39.348
I'm not talking
about technology.

00:37:39.423 --> 00:37:40.720
I'm talking about people...

00:37:40.791 --> 00:37:43.851
people who weren't as lucky
as you and me.

00:37:44.895 --> 00:37:46.522
You said you and the Doctor

00:37:46.597 --> 00:37:48.531
wanted to "keep things
in the family."

00:37:51.335 --> 00:37:55.931
But our family's
not complete anymore, is it?

00:37:56.073 --> 00:37:59.338
I'm asking you
to trust my judgment, Harry...

00:37:59.410 --> 00:38:02.208
one last time.

00:38:14.759 --> 00:38:16.386
Am I early?

00:38:16.460 --> 00:38:17.859
No, you're right on time.

00:38:17.928 --> 00:38:19.623
Something wrong with the door?

00:38:19.697 --> 00:38:21.528
I didn't think it
would be discreet

00:38:21.599 --> 00:38:25.262
to be seen carrying flowers
to the First Officer's quarters.

00:38:29.774 --> 00:38:31.071
Your research?

00:38:35.780 --> 00:38:37.907
I should put these in water.

00:38:54.165 --> 00:38:56.759
I've been told that anticipation

00:38:56.834 --> 00:39:00.668
of the first kiss
is often uncomfortable.

00:39:00.738 --> 00:39:04.003
I wanted to alleviate
the tension.

00:39:04.075 --> 00:39:07.670
That was very considerate
of you.

00:39:07.745 --> 00:39:11.340
What about the second kiss?

00:39:11.415 --> 00:39:13.542
I'd have to check the database.

00:39:13.617 --> 00:39:15.710
It may indicate...

00:39:21.092 --> 00:39:24.391
Senior officers,
report to the Bridge.

00:39:28.933 --> 00:39:33.063
Next time, we deactivate
the com system.

00:39:40.378 --> 00:39:41.310
What is it?

00:39:41.379 --> 00:39:43.210
Judging from the tachyon
emissions,

00:39:43.280 --> 00:39:45.043
some sort of temporal rift.

00:39:45.116 --> 00:39:46.708
How's it being generated?

00:39:46.784 --> 00:39:49.617
That's what we're trying
to figure out.

00:39:54.992 --> 00:39:58.723
If Starfleet Command finds out
I had anything to do with this,

00:39:58.796 --> 00:40:00.764
they'll demote me
back to Ensign.

00:40:00.831 --> 00:40:02.128
You worry too much, Harry.

00:40:02.199 --> 00:40:03.325
It's turning you gray.

00:40:05.302 --> 00:40:09.898
Propulsion's on line.
Plasma flow stable.

00:40:14.812 --> 00:40:17.940
This device of Korath's...

00:40:18.082 --> 00:40:20.550
it produces too much
tachyokinetic energy.

00:40:20.618 --> 00:40:22.085
It could burn itself out

00:40:22.153 --> 00:40:24.849
by the time you get
where you're going.

00:40:27.992 --> 00:40:29.789
You wouldn't be able
to get back.

00:40:29.860 --> 00:40:33.455
I always assumed
it was a one-way trip.

00:40:39.170 --> 00:40:41.866
You're sure I can't talk you
out of this?

00:40:50.014 --> 00:40:51.106
Right.

00:40:51.182 --> 00:40:53.980
Stupid question.

00:41:06.664 --> 00:41:09.064
Kim to the Rhode Island.

00:41:09.133 --> 00:41:11.431
One to beam back.

00:41:21.078 --> 00:41:23.342
Computer, activate
the chrono-deflector.

00:41:31.021 --> 00:41:32.579
Deploy armor.

00:41:32.656 --> 00:41:33.918
Unable to comply.

00:41:33.991 --> 00:41:36.016
Ablative generator is off-line.

00:41:37.094 --> 00:41:39.790
Evasive pattern, Beta-6.

00:41:39.864 --> 00:41:41.957
Open a channel
to the Rhode Island.

00:41:42.099 --> 00:41:43.896
Harry, I'm under attack.

00:41:43.968 --> 00:41:45.560
How fast can you get back here?

00:41:45.636 --> 00:41:49.231
I'm detecting nadion discharges
on the other side of the rift.

00:41:49.306 --> 00:41:50.568
Weapons fire?

00:41:50.641 --> 00:41:51.835
It's possible.

00:41:51.909 --> 00:41:53.934
The signature appears
to be Klingon.

00:41:54.011 --> 00:41:56.571
Red Alert.

00:42:01.919 --> 00:42:04.080
Stand by for transport, Admiral.

00:42:04.154 --> 00:42:07.920
You know where I'm going, Harry,
and it's not to your ship.

00:42:08.025 --> 00:42:10.186
Your structural integrity
is failing.

00:42:10.261 --> 00:42:12.422
Just get these Klingons
off my tail.

00:42:17.001 --> 00:42:19.629
Computer,
activate the tachyon pulse

00:42:19.703 --> 00:42:23.969
and direct it to these spatial
and temporal coordinates.

00:42:31.015 --> 00:42:33.381
There's a vessel
coming through the rift.

00:42:33.450 --> 00:42:34.610
Klingon?

00:42:34.685 --> 00:42:36.949
No.

00:42:37.021 --> 00:42:38.886
Federation.

00:42:46.030 --> 00:42:47.793
We're being hailed.

00:42:49.166 --> 00:42:51.828
On screen.

00:42:52.469 --> 00:42:54.164
Recalibrate your deflector

00:42:54.238 --> 00:42:56.138
to emit an anti-tachyon pulse.

00:42:56.206 --> 00:42:58.367
You have to seal that rift.

00:42:58.442 --> 00:43:01.206
It's usually considered polite
to introduce yourself

00:43:01.278 --> 00:43:02.905
before you start giving orders.

00:43:03.047 --> 00:43:06.574
Captain, a Klingon vessel
is coming through.

00:43:06.650 --> 00:43:08.481
Close the rift!

00:43:08.552 --> 00:43:12.318
In case you didn't notice,
I outrank you, Captain.

00:43:12.389 --> 00:43:14.323
Now do it.

00:43:23.367 --> 00:43:25.130
I did what you asked.

00:43:25.202 --> 00:43:28.194
Now tell me what the hell
is going on.

00:43:28.272 --> 00:43:32.140
I've come to bring Voyager home.

00:44:00.504 --> 00:44:02.495
Welcome aboard.

00:44:02.573 --> 00:44:05.599
It's good to be back.

00:44:10.014 --> 00:44:11.276
Fresh coffee.

00:44:11.348 --> 00:44:12.440
Would you like a cup?

00:44:12.516 --> 00:44:14.677
No, I gave it up years ago.

00:44:14.752 --> 00:44:16.413
I only drink tea now.

00:44:16.487 --> 00:44:17.920
I told the curator

00:44:18.022 --> 00:44:19.922
at the museum that if he wanted
to make the ready room

00:44:20.024 --> 00:44:21.889
more authentic,
he should always keep

00:44:21.959 --> 00:44:23.517
a steaming pot of coffee
on the desk.

00:44:23.594 --> 00:44:25.858
Voyager's in a museum?

00:44:25.929 --> 00:44:30.298
Voyager is a museum...
on the grounds of the Presidio.

00:44:30.367 --> 00:44:34.531
On a clear morning,
you can see Alcatraz from here.

00:44:34.605 --> 00:44:36.698
You made it back to Earth.

00:44:36.774 --> 00:44:40.801
Unfortunately, our favorite cup

00:44:40.878 --> 00:44:43.142
took a bit of a beating
along the way.

00:44:43.213 --> 00:44:47.047
It was damaged during a battle
with the Fen Domar.

00:44:47.117 --> 00:44:48.049
Who?

00:44:48.118 --> 00:44:50.484
You'll run into them
in a few years.

00:44:50.554 --> 00:44:51.578
You know what?

00:44:51.655 --> 00:44:53.957
I shouldn't be listening
to details about the future.

00:44:54.024 --> 00:44:56.549
Oh, the almighty
Temporal Prime Directive.

00:44:56.627 --> 00:44:57.559
Take my advice.

00:44:57.628 --> 00:45:00.495
It's less of a headache
if you just ignore it.

00:45:00.564 --> 00:45:03.897
You've obviously decided
to, or you wouldn't be here.

00:45:04.001 --> 00:45:06.765
A lot's happened to me
since I was you.

00:45:06.837 --> 00:45:10.034
Well, I'm still me,
and this is still my ship,

00:45:10.107 --> 00:45:12.769
so no more talk about
what's going to happen

00:45:12.843 --> 00:45:16.006
until I decide
otherwise, understood?

00:45:16.080 --> 00:45:19.481
All right.

00:45:19.550 --> 00:45:21.882
Let's talk about the past.

00:45:21.952 --> 00:45:26.355
Three days ago, you detected
elevated neutrino emissions

00:45:26.423 --> 00:45:28.323
in a nebula in Grid 986.

00:45:28.392 --> 00:45:31.088
You thought it
might be a way home.

00:45:31.161 --> 00:45:34.460
You were right.

00:45:34.531 --> 00:45:35.793
I've come to tell you

00:45:35.866 --> 00:45:37.925
to take Voyager
back to that nebula.

00:45:38.001 --> 00:45:40.196
It was crawling with Borg.

00:45:40.270 --> 00:45:42.534
I've brought technology
that'll get us past them.

00:45:42.606 --> 00:45:44.597
Oh, I don't blame you

00:45:44.675 --> 00:45:45.869
for being skeptical,

00:45:45.943 --> 00:45:48.639
but if you can't trust
yourself, who can you trust?

00:45:48.712 --> 00:45:50.236
For the sake of argument,

00:45:50.314 --> 00:45:53.442
let's say I believe everything
you're telling me.

00:45:53.517 --> 00:45:55.485
The future you come from
sounds pretty good.

00:45:55.552 --> 00:45:58.316
Voyager's home.
I'm an Admiral.

00:45:58.388 --> 00:46:01.186
There are ways
to defend against the Borg.

00:46:01.258 --> 00:46:04.318
My ready room even gets
preserved for posterity.

00:46:04.394 --> 00:46:05.884
So, why would you

00:46:05.963 --> 00:46:09.626
want to tamper with
such a rosy timeline?

00:46:09.700 --> 00:46:11.031
To answer that,

00:46:11.101 --> 00:46:15.595
I'd have to tell you more
than you want to know...

00:46:15.672 --> 00:46:17.333
but suffice it to say...

00:46:17.407 --> 00:46:20.171
if you don't do
what I'm suggesting,

00:46:20.244 --> 00:46:23.111
it's going to take you
another 16 years

00:46:23.180 --> 00:46:25.114
to get this ship home,

00:46:25.182 --> 00:46:29.414
and there are going to be
casualties along the way.

00:46:30.487 --> 00:46:33.650
I know exactly
what you're thinking.

00:46:33.724 --> 00:46:35.658
You've also become a telepath?

00:46:35.726 --> 00:46:38.923
I used to be you, remember?

00:46:39.029 --> 00:46:41.088
You're asking yourself,

00:46:41.165 --> 00:46:44.396
"Is she really
who she says she is,

00:46:44.468 --> 00:46:47.699
or is this some sort
of deception?"

00:46:47.771 --> 00:46:49.261
For all you know,
I could be a member

00:46:49.339 --> 00:46:52.672
of Species 8472 in disguise.

00:46:54.711 --> 00:46:57.305
Have your people
examine my shuttle.

00:46:57.381 --> 00:46:58.814
Tell them to take a close look

00:46:58.882 --> 00:47:02.716
at the weapon systems
and the armor technology.

00:47:02.786 --> 00:47:07.314
In the meantime, the Doctor
can confirm my identity.

00:47:07.391 --> 00:47:09.222
My scans of the Admiral's
cerebral cortex

00:47:09.293 --> 00:47:10.487
turned up
something interesting.

00:47:10.561 --> 00:47:12.051
What is it?

00:47:12.129 --> 00:47:15.860
I'm not sure... I've never seen
this kind of implant before.

00:47:15.933 --> 00:47:17.127
Alien technology?

00:47:17.201 --> 00:47:21.228
The microcircuitry
has a Starfleet signature.

00:47:21.305 --> 00:47:22.237
Of course it does.

00:47:22.306 --> 00:47:24.797
Admiral?

00:47:24.875 --> 00:47:30.279
You invented it... 12 years ago
from my perspective.

00:47:30.347 --> 00:47:33.748
I'm sorry, Admiral,
I didn't realize...

00:47:33.817 --> 00:47:35.478
What, that I was eavesdropping?

00:47:35.552 --> 00:47:38.043
I may be old, but my hearing's
still excellent,

00:47:38.121 --> 00:47:40.589
thanks to your exemplary care
over the years.

00:47:41.658 --> 00:47:43.785
So, this...

00:47:43.861 --> 00:47:45.886
implant I'm going to invent...

00:47:45.963 --> 00:47:47.897
what does it do?

00:47:47.965 --> 00:47:49.865
It's a synaptic transceiver.

00:47:49.933 --> 00:47:52.925
It allows me to pilot a vessel

00:47:53.036 --> 00:47:56.301
equipped with a neural
interface.

00:47:56.373 --> 00:47:58.068
Fascinating.

00:47:58.141 --> 00:47:59.073
Tell me...

00:47:59.142 --> 00:48:00.632
what other extraordinary
breakthroughs

00:48:00.711 --> 00:48:02.235
- am I going to make?
- Doctor.

00:48:02.312 --> 00:48:03.870
Sorry, Captain,
but you can't blame

00:48:03.981 --> 00:48:05.107
a hologram for being curious.

00:48:05.182 --> 00:48:07.980
Just finish your report.

00:48:08.051 --> 00:48:11.214
Yes, ma'am.

00:48:13.590 --> 00:48:17.458
My scans indicate the two of you
are genetically identical.

00:48:17.527 --> 00:48:21.896
The Admiral is you,
approximately 26 years from now.

00:48:25.168 --> 00:48:27.295
Hello, Seven.

00:48:32.009 --> 00:48:33.567
The technology aboard
the Admiral's ship

00:48:33.644 --> 00:48:35.111
is impressive.

00:48:35.178 --> 00:48:36.577
Much of it appears
to have been designed

00:48:36.647 --> 00:48:39.081
to defend against the Borg.

00:48:39.149 --> 00:48:41.447
Could we install these
systems on Voyager?

00:48:41.518 --> 00:48:43.611
The stealth technology
is incompatible,

00:48:43.687 --> 00:48:46.417
but I believe we can adapt
the armor and weapons.

00:48:47.491 --> 00:48:49.823
Well, Captain?

00:48:55.198 --> 00:48:57.496
Do it.

00:49:01.772 --> 00:49:07.574
Captain's Personal Log,
Stardate 54973.4.

00:49:07.644 --> 00:49:09.635
We've begun outfitting Voyager

00:49:09.713 --> 00:49:11.578
with Admiral Janeway's upgrades.

00:49:11.648 --> 00:49:14.412
As soon as the major
modifications are complete,

00:49:14.484 --> 00:49:17.248
we'll reverse course
and head back to the nebula.

00:49:17.321 --> 00:49:20.757
Though I've had some strange
experiences in my career,

00:49:20.824 --> 00:49:22.257
nothing quite compares

00:49:22.326 --> 00:49:25.420
to the sight of my future self
briefing my officers

00:49:25.495 --> 00:49:29.431
on technology
that hasn't been invented yet.

00:49:33.337 --> 00:49:36.795
Computer, begin
regeneration cycle.

00:49:41.345 --> 00:49:43.279
Seven of Nine,

00:49:43.347 --> 00:49:47.545
Tertiary Adjunct
of Unimatrix Zero One.

00:49:47.617 --> 00:49:50.051
It's been too long.

00:49:50.120 --> 00:49:52.179
What do you want?

00:49:52.255 --> 00:49:54.689
Do I need a reason
to visit a friend?

00:49:54.758 --> 00:49:56.885
We're not friends.

00:49:56.960 --> 00:49:59.451
No...

00:49:59.529 --> 00:50:03.295
we're more than that.

00:50:03.367 --> 00:50:05.494
We're family.

00:50:05.569 --> 00:50:09.266
While we're on the subject
of old friends...

00:50:09.339 --> 00:50:13.537
I see that Voyager has
just gotten a visitor,

00:50:13.610 --> 00:50:16.738
and she's come from the future.

00:50:16.813 --> 00:50:18.337
Tell me why.

00:50:18.415 --> 00:50:22.146
You may be able to communicate
with me while I'm regenerating,

00:50:22.219 --> 00:50:24.153
but I'm no longer a drone.

00:50:24.221 --> 00:50:26.485
I don't answer to you.

00:50:31.895 --> 00:50:35.626
I've extrapolated
Voyager's trajectory.

00:50:35.699 --> 00:50:39.726
I know that you're
returning to the nebula.

00:50:39.803 --> 00:50:42.294
I suggest you alter course.

00:50:42.372 --> 00:50:44.101
Why should we comply?

00:50:46.676 --> 00:50:51.170
You've always been
my favorite, Seven.

00:50:51.248 --> 00:50:55.651
In spite of their
obvious imperfections,

00:50:55.719 --> 00:50:59.985
I know how much you care
for the Voyager crew...

00:51:00.057 --> 00:51:04.255
so I've left them alone.

00:51:04.327 --> 00:51:06.921
Imagine... how you would feel

00:51:06.997 --> 00:51:10.933
if I were forced
to assimilate them.

00:51:11.001 --> 00:51:13.765
Voyager is no threat
to the collective.

00:51:13.837 --> 00:51:16.271
We simply want to return
to the Alpha Quadrant.

00:51:16.339 --> 00:51:19.433
I've no objection to that...

00:51:19.509 --> 00:51:23.445
but if you try to enter
my nebula again...

00:51:23.513 --> 00:51:26.414
I'll destroy you.

00:51:31.021 --> 00:51:35.151
Warning. Regeneration cycle
incomplete.

00:51:39.863 --> 00:51:43.629
Her cortical node was exposed
to a low-energy EM surge.

00:51:43.700 --> 00:51:45.930
It could've been much worse.

00:51:46.002 --> 00:51:47.264
It was the Borg Queen.

00:51:47.337 --> 00:51:48.702
She wanted to make sure

00:51:48.772 --> 00:51:50.706
I'd be able
to deliver a message.

00:51:50.774 --> 00:51:52.708
She said she'd
assimilate Voyager

00:51:52.776 --> 00:51:54.971
if we attempted
to reenter the nebula.

00:51:55.078 --> 00:51:57.103
Why is it so important to her?

00:51:57.180 --> 00:51:58.306
That doesn't matter.

00:51:58.381 --> 00:52:01.179
She's not going to be able
to make good on her threat.

00:52:01.251 --> 00:52:02.411
I wish I shared your confidence.

00:52:02.486 --> 00:52:03.510
You would, if you'd had

00:52:03.587 --> 00:52:06.283
as much experience
with the Queen as I've had.

00:52:06.356 --> 00:52:10.258
It was one thing to attempt this
when we thought it was a secret,

00:52:10.327 --> 00:52:11.760
but if the Borg are
monitoring us...

00:52:11.828 --> 00:52:13.762
There's no guarantee
they won't try to assimilate

00:52:13.830 --> 00:52:17.129
Voyager even if we don't go
back into the nebula.

00:52:17.200 --> 00:52:18.929
Is that supposed to be
reassuring?

00:52:19.069 --> 00:52:21.594
I'm not saying
the Borg aren't dangerous,

00:52:21.671 --> 00:52:23.104
but from my perspective,

00:52:23.173 --> 00:52:25.937
they're 30 years
behind the times.

00:52:26.042 --> 00:52:27.669
We shouldn't push our luck.

00:52:27.744 --> 00:52:30.269
Luck's not going to have
anything to do with it.

00:52:30.347 --> 00:52:31.609
I know...
you don't want to hear

00:52:31.681 --> 00:52:33.273
too much about the future,

00:52:33.350 --> 00:52:35.443
but let's just say
I ran into the Borg

00:52:35.519 --> 00:52:38.613
a few more times
before I made it home.

00:52:38.688 --> 00:52:40.952
If I hadn't developed
technology and tactics

00:52:41.024 --> 00:52:42.616
that could defeat them,

00:52:42.692 --> 00:52:45.559
I wouldn't be
standing here today.

00:52:50.834 --> 00:52:53.166
We'll maintain course
for the nebula,

00:52:53.236 --> 00:52:55.727
but we'll stay
at Red Alert, and I want

00:52:55.805 --> 00:52:57.966
continuous scans
for Borg activity.

00:53:07.184 --> 00:53:09.914
I heard what happened.
Are you all right?

00:53:09.986 --> 00:53:11.419
I'm fine.

00:53:11.488 --> 00:53:13.820
Because if you need
time to rest...

00:53:13.890 --> 00:53:16.586
I am in charge
of the duty roster.

00:53:16.660 --> 00:53:17.888
It would be inappropriate

00:53:17.961 --> 00:53:19.622
to allow our personal
relationship

00:53:19.696 --> 00:53:21.391
to affect
your command decisions.

00:53:22.465 --> 00:53:23.727
You're right.

00:53:23.800 --> 00:53:26.098
This is a time to keep
things professional.

00:53:26.169 --> 00:53:27.761
Report.

00:53:27.837 --> 00:53:31.102
There's no sign of Borg activity
within a ten light-year radius.

00:53:31.174 --> 00:53:33.438
That's good news, crewman.

00:53:33.510 --> 00:53:35.239
Yes, sir,

00:53:35.312 --> 00:53:38.440
but we shouldn't
underestimate the collective.

00:53:38.515 --> 00:53:42.212
The Admiral seems confident
we can make it past them.

00:53:42.285 --> 00:53:44.549
Captain Janeway
is more cautious.

00:53:44.621 --> 00:53:46.486
Our chances would be good

00:53:46.556 --> 00:53:49.787
with one Kathryn Janeway
on the Bridge, but with two...

00:53:49.859 --> 00:53:52.327
I'd bet on this ship any day.

00:53:58.034 --> 00:54:03.404
If we do make it back to Earth,
what are your plans?

00:54:06.109 --> 00:54:10.045
I assume Starfleet
will want to debrief me.

00:54:10.113 --> 00:54:12.809
And then, I suppose,
I'll attempt to find

00:54:12.882 --> 00:54:14.747
a useful position somewhere.

00:54:17.554 --> 00:54:19.522
You?

00:54:19.589 --> 00:54:22.786
I don't know yet, either.

00:54:22.859 --> 00:54:26.260
But wherever I end up...

00:54:26.329 --> 00:54:29.958
I'm going to make sure it's
in transporter range of you.

00:54:33.203 --> 00:54:35.103
I don't want this
whole system crashing

00:54:35.171 --> 00:54:36.934
because of one faulty relay.

00:54:37.007 --> 00:54:38.599
- Install new ones.
- Yes, ma'am.

00:54:38.675 --> 00:54:41.269
And I need an update on
the inductor capacitance.

00:54:41.344 --> 00:54:42.606
- B'Elanna.
- Yes, Lieutenant.

00:54:42.679 --> 00:54:44.271
Shouldn't you be on the Bridge?

00:54:44.347 --> 00:54:46.281
Is there something wrong
with the pilot requesting

00:54:46.349 --> 00:54:47.941
a systems report
from the Chief Engineer?

00:54:48.018 --> 00:54:48.950
The last report I got

00:54:49.019 --> 00:54:50.953
said the com system
was working perfectly.

00:54:51.021 --> 00:54:52.784
Okay, you caught me.

00:54:52.856 --> 00:54:53.948
I'm checking up on you.

00:54:54.024 --> 00:54:55.116
I'm fine.

00:54:55.191 --> 00:54:56.283
Your back?

00:54:56.359 --> 00:54:57.621
I'm ignoring it.

00:54:57.694 --> 00:55:01.130
Well, I would offer to give you
a massage, but then...

00:55:01.197 --> 00:55:02.562
everybody would want one.

00:55:02.632 --> 00:55:06.227
You know, for a Starfleet
flyboy, you're pretty sweet.

00:55:06.303 --> 00:55:08.237
So, how's it going?

00:55:08.305 --> 00:55:11.399
This armor technology
that the Admiral brought...

00:55:11.474 --> 00:55:12.736
it's incredible.

00:55:12.809 --> 00:55:14.242
I hate to sound like Harry,

00:55:14.311 --> 00:55:15.744
but we might actually
make it this time.

00:55:15.812 --> 00:55:18.406
Well, you don't seem
too happy about that.

00:55:18.481 --> 00:55:19.914
Oh, I'm happy.

00:55:19.983 --> 00:55:22.417
It's just that I'd actually
gotten used to the idea

00:55:22.485 --> 00:55:24.248
of raising our daughter
on Voyager,

00:55:24.321 --> 00:55:26.255
and now I might end up
delivering her

00:55:26.323 --> 00:55:29.258
at Starfleet Medical
instead of Sick Bay.

00:55:29.326 --> 00:55:31.920
Well, that wouldn't
be so bad, would it?

00:55:31.995 --> 00:55:34.259
Not as long as you're with me...

00:55:34.331 --> 00:55:35.923
and I want the Doctor.

00:55:35.999 --> 00:55:37.432
I don't want some stranger.

00:55:37.500 --> 00:55:40.765
You would have to take him
off-line to keep him away.

00:55:40.837 --> 00:55:42.771
If we do make it home...

00:55:42.839 --> 00:55:44.898
where do you think we'll live?

00:55:44.974 --> 00:55:48.876
Well, we could always stay
with my parents for a while.

00:55:48.945 --> 00:55:50.845
You're right.
Bad idea.

00:55:50.914 --> 00:55:52.779
Of course, it probably
doesn't matter to you anyway.

00:55:52.849 --> 00:55:54.441
You flyboys are all the same.

00:55:54.517 --> 00:55:56.917
You'll probably take the
first piloting assignment

00:55:56.986 --> 00:55:59.750
that comes along and leave me
home to change the diapers.

00:55:59.823 --> 00:56:02.986
Not a chance.

00:56:12.569 --> 00:56:13.900
Bridge to Engineering.

00:56:13.970 --> 00:56:15.232
Go ahead, Captain.

00:56:15.305 --> 00:56:16.567
Deploy armor.

00:56:16.639 --> 00:56:18.436
Yes, ma'am.

00:56:39.529 --> 00:56:42.430
Armor integrity at 97 percent.

00:56:52.876 --> 00:56:54.070
Tuvok?

00:56:54.144 --> 00:56:56.135
Integrity holding at 90 percent.

00:56:56.212 --> 00:56:58.806
Maintain course.

00:57:04.454 --> 00:57:08.185
They're looking for ways
to adapt.

00:57:15.498 --> 00:57:16.988
Port armor integrity
down to 50 percent.

00:57:17.066 --> 00:57:18.897
40 percent.

00:57:20.970 --> 00:57:23.370
Mr. Paris,
attack pattern Alpha-1.

00:57:23.440 --> 00:57:24.737
Target the lead cube

00:57:24.808 --> 00:57:26.742
and fire transphasic torpedoes.

00:57:35.819 --> 00:57:37.810
Target the second cube.

00:57:51.267 --> 00:57:52.700
Distance to the center?

00:57:52.769 --> 00:57:55.135
Less than 100,000 kilometers.

00:58:09.619 --> 00:58:11.780
What the hell is it?

00:58:11.855 --> 00:58:14.449
Mr. Paris, alter course
to enter the aperture

00:58:14.524 --> 00:58:16.651
at coordinates 346 by 42.

00:58:16.726 --> 00:58:17.852
Belay that.

00:58:17.927 --> 00:58:19.554
I asked you a question.

00:58:19.629 --> 00:58:21.096
What is it?

00:58:21.164 --> 00:58:22.995
The road home.

00:58:23.066 --> 00:58:25.227
It's more than that.

00:58:25.301 --> 00:58:27.462
It's a transwarp hub.

00:58:27.537 --> 00:58:30.870
You once told me there were
only six of them in the galaxy.

00:58:30.940 --> 00:58:32.874
That's correct.

00:58:35.578 --> 00:58:39.105
You knew this was here,
but you didn't tell me about it.

00:58:39.182 --> 00:58:40.911
- Why?
- I'll answer all your questions

00:58:41.017 --> 00:58:44.282
once we're back
in the Alpha Quadrant.

00:58:44.354 --> 00:58:45.719
Take us out

00:58:45.788 --> 00:58:47.653
- of the nebula.
- Captain?

00:58:47.724 --> 00:58:49.487
You heard me.

00:58:49.559 --> 00:58:51.891
I gave you an order,
Lieutenant... proceed

00:58:51.961 --> 00:58:53.360
to the aperture.

00:58:53.429 --> 00:58:54.418
This is my Bridge, Admiral,

00:58:54.497 --> 00:58:56.021
and I'll have you removed,
if necessary.

00:58:56.099 --> 00:58:57.066
Take us out.

00:59:01.037 --> 00:59:02.732
Aye, Captain.

00:59:12.982 --> 00:59:15.246
This hub connects with thousands
of transwarp conduits

00:59:15.318 --> 00:59:18.719
with end points
in all four Quadrants.

00:59:18.788 --> 00:59:20.187
It allows the collective
to deploy vessels

00:59:20.256 --> 00:59:21.780
almost anywhere in the galaxy
within minutes.

00:59:21.858 --> 00:59:25.157
Of all the Borg's
tactical advantages,

00:59:25.228 --> 00:59:26.991
this could be
the most significant.

00:59:27.063 --> 00:59:29.588
It's no wonder the Queen
didn't want us in that nebula.

00:59:29.666 --> 00:59:31.497
So, how do we destroy it?

00:59:31.568 --> 00:59:34.036
The structure is supported by

00:59:34.103 --> 00:59:36.435
a series of
interspatial manifolds.

00:59:36.506 --> 00:59:38.406
If we could disable
enough of them,

00:59:38.474 --> 00:59:40.874
theoretically,
the hub would collapse.

00:59:40.944 --> 00:59:42.206
This is a waste of time.

00:59:42.278 --> 00:59:43.905
The shielding
for those manifolds

00:59:43.980 --> 00:59:46.005
is regulated
from the central nexus

00:59:46.082 --> 00:59:47.674
by the Queen herself.

00:59:47.750 --> 00:59:49.411
You might be able
to damage one of them

00:59:49.485 --> 00:59:50.918
maybe two, but by the time

00:59:51.020 --> 00:59:52.783
you moved onto the third,
she'd adapt.

00:59:52.855 --> 00:59:55.585
There may be a way to
bring them down simultaneously.

00:59:55.658 --> 00:59:57.649
From where, inside the hub?

00:59:57.727 --> 00:59:59.592
Voyager would be crushed
like a bug.

00:59:59.662 --> 01:00:02.153
What about taking the conduit
back to the Alpha Quadrant

01:00:02.231 --> 01:00:05.257
and then destroying the
structure from the other side?

01:00:05.335 --> 01:00:06.461
This hub is here.

01:00:06.536 --> 01:00:10.028
There's nothing in the Alpha
Quadrant but exit apertures.

01:00:10.106 --> 01:00:11.937
While you're all standing around

01:00:12.041 --> 01:00:14.475
dreaming up fantasy
tactical scenarios,

01:00:14.544 --> 01:00:16.478
the Queen is studying

01:00:16.546 --> 01:00:18.571
her scans
of our armor and weapons

01:00:18.648 --> 01:00:20.548
and she's probably got
the entire collective

01:00:20.617 --> 01:00:23.279
working on a way
to counter them.

01:00:23.353 --> 01:00:27.153
So, take the ship back into
that nebula, and go home

01:00:27.223 --> 01:00:29.054
before it's too late.

01:00:29.125 --> 01:00:30.786
Find a way to destroy that hub.

01:00:30.860 --> 01:00:31.827
Let's take a walk.

01:00:35.798 --> 01:00:38.232
I want to know why you
didn't tell me about this.

01:00:38.301 --> 01:00:39.962
Because I remember
how stubborn

01:00:40.069 --> 01:00:41.866
and self-righteous
I used to be.

01:00:41.938 --> 01:00:44.168
I figured you might try
to do something stupid.

01:00:44.240 --> 01:00:45.172
We have an opportunity

01:00:45.241 --> 01:00:47.232
to deal a crippling blow
to the Borg.

01:00:47.310 --> 01:00:48.675
It could save millions of lives.

01:00:48.745 --> 01:00:50.645
I didn't spend
the last ten years

01:00:50.713 --> 01:00:52.681
looking for a way to get
this crew home earlier

01:00:52.749 --> 01:00:53.977
so you could throw it all away

01:00:54.083 --> 01:00:55.983
on some intergalactic
goodwill mission.

01:00:56.052 --> 01:00:58.145
Maybe we should go
back to Sick Bay.

01:00:58.221 --> 01:00:59.950
Why, so you can have me sedated?

01:01:00.023 --> 01:01:02.548
So I can have the Doctor
reconfirm your identity.

01:01:02.625 --> 01:01:04.092
I refuse to believe
I'll ever become

01:01:04.160 --> 01:01:05.787
as cynical as you.

01:01:05.862 --> 01:01:08.160
Am I the only one
experiencing déjà vu here?

01:01:08.231 --> 01:01:09.425
What are you talking about?

01:01:09.499 --> 01:01:10.591
Seven years ago,

01:01:10.667 --> 01:01:13.067
you had the chance to use
the Caretaker's Array

01:01:13.136 --> 01:01:14.501
to get Voyager home.

01:01:14.570 --> 01:01:15.935
Instead, you destroyed it.

01:01:16.039 --> 01:01:17.939
I did what I knew was right.

01:01:18.007 --> 01:01:19.702
You chose to put the lives
of strangers

01:01:19.776 --> 01:01:21.209
ahead of the lives of your crew.

01:01:21.277 --> 01:01:22.938
You can't make
the same mistake again.

01:01:23.046 --> 01:01:24.240
You got Voyager home,

01:01:24.313 --> 01:01:26.042
which means I will, too.

01:01:26.115 --> 01:01:28.379
If it takes a few more years,
then that's...

01:01:28.451 --> 01:01:30.476
Seven of Nine is going to die.

01:01:31.954 --> 01:01:33.182
What?

01:01:33.256 --> 01:01:34.951
Three years from now.

01:01:35.058 --> 01:01:36.855
She'll be injured
on an away mission.

01:01:36.926 --> 01:01:38.359
She'll make it back to Voyager

01:01:38.428 --> 01:01:40.862
and die in the arms
of her husband.

01:01:41.898 --> 01:01:42.830
Husband?

01:01:42.899 --> 01:01:44.560
Chakotay.

01:01:44.634 --> 01:01:47.967
He'll never be the same
after Seven's death,

01:01:48.037 --> 01:01:49.527
and neither will you.

01:01:53.609 --> 01:01:56.305
If I know
what's going to happen,

01:01:56.379 --> 01:01:58.438
I can avoid it.

01:01:58.514 --> 01:02:00.072
Seven isn't the only one.

01:02:00.149 --> 01:02:02.777
Between this day and the
day I got Voyager home,

01:02:02.852 --> 01:02:06.720
I lost 22 crew members.

01:02:06.789 --> 01:02:09.622
And then, of course,
there's Tuvok.

01:02:09.692 --> 01:02:11.125
What about him?

01:02:11.194 --> 01:02:13.662
You're forgetting the Temporal
Prime Directive, Captain.

01:02:13.730 --> 01:02:15.755
The hell with it.

01:02:15.832 --> 01:02:17.732
Fine.

01:02:17.800 --> 01:02:19.825
Tuvok has a degenerative
neurological condition

01:02:19.902 --> 01:02:22.029
that he hasn't told you about.

01:02:22.105 --> 01:02:23.663
There's a cure
in the Alpha Quadrant,

01:02:23.740 --> 01:02:26.538
but if he doesn't get it
in time...

01:02:26.609 --> 01:02:29.635
Even if you alter
Voyager's route,

01:02:29.712 --> 01:02:31.942
limit your contact
with alien species,

01:02:32.014 --> 01:02:34.744
you're going to lose people.

01:02:34.817 --> 01:02:36.910
But I'm offering you a chance

01:02:36.986 --> 01:02:40.353
to get all of them home
safe and sound, today.

01:02:40.423 --> 01:02:43.358
Are you really going
to walk away from that?

01:02:45.962 --> 01:02:49.898
Your concern is appreciated,
Captain, but premature.

01:02:49.966 --> 01:02:51.126
It will be several years

01:02:51.200 --> 01:02:53.100
before the symptoms
become serious.

01:02:53.169 --> 01:02:54.796
Until then, the Doctor

01:02:54.871 --> 01:02:57.897
can manage my condition
with medication.

01:02:57.974 --> 01:03:00.067
Is it true,
what the Admiral said...

01:03:00.143 --> 01:03:03.044
that there's a cure
in the Alpha Quadrant?

01:03:03.112 --> 01:03:06.138
It is called a fal-tor-voh

01:03:06.215 --> 01:03:08.877
and it requires a mind-meld
with another Vulcan.

01:03:08.951 --> 01:03:11.317
What about the other
Vulcans on Voyager?

01:03:11.387 --> 01:03:14.083
None of them are compatible.

01:03:14.157 --> 01:03:17.718
But members of your family are.

01:03:20.129 --> 01:03:22.256
If you knew that returning
to the Alpha Quadrant

01:03:22.331 --> 01:03:25.789
was your only chance
for recovery...

01:03:25.868 --> 01:03:27.495
why didn't you object
when I asked you

01:03:27.570 --> 01:03:29.265
to help find a way
to destroy the hub?

01:03:29.338 --> 01:03:33.707
My sense of logic
isn't impaired yet.

01:03:33.776 --> 01:03:36.802
If we succeed, millions
of lives will be saved.

01:03:38.781 --> 01:03:40.578
What about your life?

01:03:41.851 --> 01:03:44.411
To quote Ambassador Spock:

01:03:44.487 --> 01:03:47.752
"The needs of the many
outweigh the needs of the few."

01:03:49.425 --> 01:03:53.486
I appreciate your candor,
Admiral.

01:03:53.563 --> 01:03:56.157
But Captain Janeway is
my commanding officer.

01:03:56.232 --> 01:03:57.597
I won't disobey her.

01:03:57.667 --> 01:03:59.294
I'm not asking you to.

01:03:59.368 --> 01:04:01.700
I simply want you to tell
her that, in your opinion,

01:04:01.771 --> 01:04:05.764
destroying the hub is too
risky, the cost too high.

01:04:05.842 --> 01:04:06.900
I can't do that.

01:04:07.043 --> 01:04:09.841
Even if it means avoiding
the consequences I mentioned?

01:04:09.912 --> 01:04:12.039
Now that I know
about those consequences,

01:04:12.114 --> 01:04:14.275
they're no longer a certainty.

01:04:14.350 --> 01:04:15.681
But even if they were,

01:04:15.751 --> 01:04:17.446
my death would be
a small price to pay

01:04:17.520 --> 01:04:19.647
for the destruction
of the transwarp network.

01:04:19.722 --> 01:04:23.556
I have known you for
a long time, Seven...

01:04:23.626 --> 01:04:26.925
longer than you've
known yourself.

01:04:27.029 --> 01:04:29.293
You're thinking that
collapsing the network

01:04:29.365 --> 01:04:31.458
is an opportunity
to atone for atrocities

01:04:31.534 --> 01:04:34.367
you participated in
while you were a drone.

01:04:34.437 --> 01:04:35.927
It's time to let go of the past

01:04:36.038 --> 01:04:38.506
and start thinking
about your future.

01:04:38.574 --> 01:04:41.270
My future is insignificant
compared to the lives

01:04:41.344 --> 01:04:42.709
of the people we'd be saving.

01:04:42.778 --> 01:04:43.938
You're being selfish.

01:04:44.046 --> 01:04:44.944
Selfish?!

01:04:45.081 --> 01:04:46.605
I'm talking
about helping others.

01:04:46.682 --> 01:04:47.614
Strangers...

01:04:47.683 --> 01:04:50.277
in a hypothetical scenario.

01:04:50.353 --> 01:04:51.650
I'm talking about real life...

01:04:51.721 --> 01:04:55.157
your colleagues, your friends...

01:04:55.224 --> 01:04:56.782
people who love you.

01:04:56.859 --> 01:05:02.889
Imagine the impact
your death would have on them.

01:05:02.965 --> 01:05:05.559
Excuse me, Admiral.

01:05:05.635 --> 01:05:07.796
I have work to complete.

01:05:10.306 --> 01:05:13.673
Once inside, we'd fire a spread
of transphasic torpedoes.

01:05:13.743 --> 01:05:16.075
They'd be programmed to
detonate simultaneously.

01:05:16.145 --> 01:05:18.045
If the torpedoes
penetrate the shielding,

01:05:18.114 --> 01:05:19.843
the conduits should
begin to collapse

01:05:19.916 --> 01:05:21.474
in a cascade reaction.

01:05:21.550 --> 01:05:23.541
In order to avoid
the shock wave,

01:05:23.619 --> 01:05:26.281
we'd have less than ten seconds
to exit the hub.

01:05:31.794 --> 01:05:33.762
A long time ago,
I made a decision

01:05:33.829 --> 01:05:37.094
that stranded this crew
in the Delta Quadrant.

01:05:37.166 --> 01:05:40.363
I don't regret that decision,

01:05:40.436 --> 01:05:44.702
but I didn't know
all of you then,

01:05:44.774 --> 01:05:48.540
and Voyager was just a starship.

01:05:48.611 --> 01:05:51.205
It's much more than that now.

01:05:51.280 --> 01:05:55.307
It's become our home.

01:05:55.384 --> 01:05:57.614
I know I could order you
to carry out this plan

01:05:57.687 --> 01:05:58.949
and none of you would hesitate

01:05:59.021 --> 01:06:02.479
for a second,
but I'm not going to do that.

01:06:02.558 --> 01:06:05.686
You know the crewmen
who work under you

01:06:05.761 --> 01:06:08.821
and you know what
your own hearts are telling you.

01:06:08.898 --> 01:06:10.422
So we're not going
to attempt this

01:06:10.499 --> 01:06:13.297
unless everyone
in this room agrees.

01:06:13.369 --> 01:06:17.237
No one will think less
of you if you don't.

01:06:18.307 --> 01:06:19.433
Captain.

01:06:19.508 --> 01:06:22.238
Go ahead, Harry.

01:06:22.311 --> 01:06:24.336
I think it's safe to say

01:06:24.413 --> 01:06:29.510
that no one on this crew
has been more... obsessed

01:06:29.585 --> 01:06:31.746
with getting home than I have.

01:06:34.690 --> 01:06:36.658
But...

01:06:36.726 --> 01:06:38.921
when I think about

01:06:38.995 --> 01:06:40.622
everything we've been
through together

01:06:40.696 --> 01:06:46.532
maybe it's not
the destination that matters...

01:06:46.602 --> 01:06:49.435
maybe it's the journey.

01:06:49.505 --> 01:06:51.939
And if that journey
takes a little longer,

01:06:52.074 --> 01:06:55.601
so we can do something
we all believe in,

01:06:55.678 --> 01:06:58.408
I can't think of anyplace
I'd rather be

01:06:58.481 --> 01:07:02.008
or any people
I'd rather be with.

01:07:02.084 --> 01:07:04.348
To the journey.

01:07:04.420 --> 01:07:05.409
Hear, hear.

01:07:05.488 --> 01:07:06.955
To the journey.

01:07:16.866 --> 01:07:18.731
Coffee. Black.

01:07:18.801 --> 01:07:20.234
I thought you gave it up.

01:07:20.302 --> 01:07:24.864
I've decided to revive
a few of my old habits.

01:07:24.940 --> 01:07:26.271
Oh?

01:07:26.342 --> 01:07:29.436
What else besides the coffee?

01:07:29.512 --> 01:07:32.106
Oh, well...

01:07:32.181 --> 01:07:34.911
I used to be
much more idealistic.

01:07:35.017 --> 01:07:37.042
I took a lot of risks.

01:07:40.423 --> 01:07:42.687
I've been so determined
to get this crew home

01:07:42.758 --> 01:07:45.226
for so many years...

01:07:45.294 --> 01:07:49.731
that I think I forgot how much
they loved being together

01:07:49.799 --> 01:07:54.793
and how loyal they were to you.

01:07:54.870 --> 01:07:58.772
It's taken me a few days
to realize it.

01:07:58.841 --> 01:08:01.901
This is your ship,

01:08:01.977 --> 01:08:05.378
your crew... not mine.

01:08:05.448 --> 01:08:07.712
I was wrong to lie to you,

01:08:07.783 --> 01:08:10.081
to think I could talk you
out of something

01:08:10.152 --> 01:08:11.642
you'd set your mind to.

01:08:11.720 --> 01:08:12.982
You were only trying to do

01:08:13.055 --> 01:08:15.114
what you thought was right
for all of us.

01:08:15.191 --> 01:08:17.716
Well, you've changed
my mind about that.

01:08:23.165 --> 01:08:26.191
And I'd like to help you
carry out your mission.

01:08:26.268 --> 01:08:29.431
Maybe together we can
increase our odds.

01:08:29.505 --> 01:08:32.030
Maybe we can do more than that.

01:08:32.108 --> 01:08:33.905
There's got to be

01:08:33.976 --> 01:08:36.206
a way to have our cake
and eat it, too.

01:08:36.278 --> 01:08:40.214
We can't destroy the hub
and get Voyager home.

01:08:44.353 --> 01:08:47.481
Are you absolutely sure
about that?

01:08:49.625 --> 01:08:52.321
There might be a way.

01:08:52.394 --> 01:08:55.830
I considered it once,
but it seemed too risky.

01:08:55.898 --> 01:08:59.299
That was before you decided
to revive your old habits.

01:09:03.105 --> 01:09:05.801
I don't know why
I ever gave this up.

01:09:10.379 --> 01:09:11.778
It's about time.

01:09:11.847 --> 01:09:13.815
I'm not getting any younger,
you know.

01:09:19.655 --> 01:09:22.681
You're sure you want to do this?

01:09:22.758 --> 01:09:25.192
No...

01:09:25.261 --> 01:09:27.855
but Voyager isn't big enough
for both of us.

01:09:39.308 --> 01:09:40.832
Good luck, Admiral.

01:09:40.910 --> 01:09:43.242
You, too.

01:09:44.914 --> 01:09:47.041
Captain...

01:09:49.251 --> 01:09:52.220
I'm glad I got
to know you again.

01:10:19.114 --> 01:10:21.776
Any word from the Admiral?

01:10:21.850 --> 01:10:24.444
We lost contact as soon
as she entered the hub.

01:10:24.520 --> 01:10:26.420
Did the Borg give her
any trouble?

01:10:26.488 --> 01:10:28.183
Her vessel was scanned
by several cubes,

01:10:28.257 --> 01:10:30.088
but none approached her... sir.

01:10:32.828 --> 01:10:35.490
Are we keeping things
professional again today?

01:10:35.564 --> 01:10:36.826
Yes, Commander.

01:10:40.903 --> 01:10:43.599
You're not joking, are you?

01:10:43.672 --> 01:10:44.866
No.

01:10:51.814 --> 01:10:52.838
What's wrong?

01:10:52.915 --> 01:10:55.713
Nothing.
I'm just... busy.

01:10:57.786 --> 01:11:02.416
I think I've gotten to know you
a little better than that.

01:11:02.491 --> 01:11:04.152
I'd prefer it if you
didn't speak to me

01:11:04.226 --> 01:11:05.557
as though we're
on intimate terms.

01:11:05.628 --> 01:11:09.189
We are on intimate terms.

01:11:09.265 --> 01:11:10.323
Not anymore.

01:11:11.834 --> 01:11:14.325
What the hell is going on?

01:11:14.403 --> 01:11:15.631
I've decided to alter

01:11:15.704 --> 01:11:17.604
the parameters
of our relationship.

01:11:17.673 --> 01:11:20.506
You mind telling me why?

01:11:20.576 --> 01:11:23.238
We both have dangerous
occupations.

01:11:23.312 --> 01:11:24.643
It's possible one of us

01:11:24.713 --> 01:11:27.580
could be seriously
injured or worse.

01:11:27.650 --> 01:11:32.587
I believe it's best
to avoid emotional attachments.

01:11:32.655 --> 01:11:35.749
Maybe you can just
flip some Borg switch

01:11:35.824 --> 01:11:38.258
and shut down your
emotions, but I can't.

01:11:38.327 --> 01:11:39.954
I suggest you try.

01:11:40.062 --> 01:11:42.860
It will make things
less difficult for you

01:11:42.931 --> 01:11:45.422
if any harm should come to me.

01:11:45.501 --> 01:11:48.493
Why are you suddenly
so concerned about that?

01:11:48.570 --> 01:11:50.265
Is there something
I should know?

01:11:55.611 --> 01:12:00.378
The Admiral suggested...

01:12:00.449 --> 01:12:02.474
that your feelings for me

01:12:02.551 --> 01:12:05.520
will cause you pain
in the future.

01:12:07.890 --> 01:12:10.290
I can't allow that to happen.

01:12:10.359 --> 01:12:14.090
Seven...

01:12:14.163 --> 01:12:18.156
any relationship involves risk

01:12:18.233 --> 01:12:19.632
and nobody can guarantee

01:12:19.702 --> 01:12:21.829
what's going to happen
tomorrow...

01:12:21.904 --> 01:12:24.429
not even an Admiral
from the future.

01:12:28.711 --> 01:12:29.735
The only certainty

01:12:29.812 --> 01:12:33.145
is how we feel about each other
here and now.

01:12:33.215 --> 01:12:34.944
If you think I'm going
to let you end this

01:12:35.084 --> 01:12:39.418
because of what might happen...

01:12:39.488 --> 01:12:42.321
then you need to get to
know me a little better.

01:12:56.572 --> 01:12:57.630
Try to relax, Lieutenant.

01:12:57.706 --> 01:12:59.367
Oh, if you tell me
to relax one more time

01:12:59.441 --> 01:13:01.238
I'm going to rip your
holographic head off!

01:13:01.310 --> 01:13:02.242
I hope you don't intend

01:13:02.311 --> 01:13:03.676
to kiss your baby
with that mouth.

01:13:03.746 --> 01:13:05.805
Tell me this isn't
another false alarm.

01:13:05.881 --> 01:13:07.576
This isn't another false alarm.

01:13:07.649 --> 01:13:08.911
I can't believe it.

01:13:09.017 --> 01:13:10.746
Oh, believe it.

01:13:10.819 --> 01:13:12.116
I might actually win.

01:13:12.187 --> 01:13:13.119
What?

01:13:13.188 --> 01:13:14.280
The baby pool.

01:13:14.356 --> 01:13:16.017
I picked today, 1500 hours.

01:13:16.091 --> 01:13:18.389
I'm so glad I could
accommodate you.

01:13:18.460 --> 01:13:19.620
Don't celebrate yet.

01:13:19.695 --> 01:13:21.822
Klingon labor sometimes
lasts several days.

01:13:23.465 --> 01:13:25.399
Of course I'm sure that
won't be the case here.

01:13:25.467 --> 01:13:27.435
Bridge to Lieutenant Paris.

01:13:27.503 --> 01:13:28.936
We're ready to get underway.

01:13:29.004 --> 01:13:30.266
Captain, I'm afraid...

01:13:30.339 --> 01:13:32.170
Go.

01:13:32.241 --> 01:13:34.368
- But...
- No "buts," flyboy.

01:13:34.443 --> 01:13:36.070
If this mission
is going to succeed,

01:13:36.145 --> 01:13:38.409
we need our best pilot
at the helm.

01:13:38.480 --> 01:13:39.947
Don't worry...

01:13:40.015 --> 01:13:41.505
the Doctor will be here with me.

01:13:41.583 --> 01:13:44.074
Is there a problem, Mr. Paris?

01:13:47.489 --> 01:13:49.514
On my way, Captain.

01:14:05.174 --> 01:14:07.142
Let's get this show on the road.

01:14:13.816 --> 01:14:17.149
Voyager has altered course.

01:14:17.219 --> 01:14:21.178
Current position,
spatial grid 362.

01:14:21.256 --> 01:14:24.885
Trajectory 112 mark 5.

01:14:24.960 --> 01:14:27.428
I don't know how you do it.

01:14:27.496 --> 01:14:30.795
All those voices
talking at once.

01:14:30.866 --> 01:14:33.357
You must get terrible headaches.

01:14:33.435 --> 01:14:36.927
If you're calling drones
to assimilate me, don't bother.

01:14:37.039 --> 01:14:41.499
I don't need drones
to assimilate you.

01:14:45.714 --> 01:14:49.844
I'm not actually here,
Your Majesty.

01:14:49.918 --> 01:14:51.613
I'm in your mind.

01:14:51.687 --> 01:14:54.952
I'm using a synaptic interface.

01:14:55.090 --> 01:14:56.819
If I were you,
I wouldn't waste my time

01:14:56.892 --> 01:14:58.450
trying to trace the signal.

01:14:58.527 --> 01:15:02.088
For the moment, it's
beyond your abilities.

01:15:06.502 --> 01:15:08.367
What do you want?

01:15:08.437 --> 01:15:10.905
To make a deal.

01:15:11.039 --> 01:15:13.030
Captain Janeway thinks I'm here

01:15:13.108 --> 01:15:15.838
to help her destroy
your transwarp network.

01:15:15.911 --> 01:15:17.538
That's beyond your abilities.

01:15:17.613 --> 01:15:18.705
Oh, I know that,

01:15:18.780 --> 01:15:22.341
and I tried to explain it
to my naive younger self,

01:15:22.417 --> 01:15:25.909
but she wouldn't listen.

01:15:25.988 --> 01:15:28.616
She's determined
to bring down that hub.

01:15:28.690 --> 01:15:30.317
She'll fail.

01:15:30.392 --> 01:15:32.622
Yes.

01:15:32.694 --> 01:15:35.925
But she has weapons that
I brought from the future.

01:15:36.064 --> 01:15:38.589
I believe you're
familiar with them.

01:15:38.667 --> 01:15:41.659
Transphasic torpedoes.

01:15:41.737 --> 01:15:43.227
We will adapt.

01:15:43.305 --> 01:15:44.932
Eventually...

01:15:45.073 --> 01:15:50.375
but not before Voyager
does a great deal of damage.

01:15:50.445 --> 01:15:51.469
I'm willing to tell you

01:15:51.547 --> 01:15:54.038
how to adapt
to those weapons now.

01:15:54.116 --> 01:15:57.745
In exchange... for what?

01:15:57.819 --> 01:16:03.724
Send a cube
to tractor Voyager...

01:16:03.792 --> 01:16:07.284
and drag them back
to the Alpha Quadrant.

01:16:11.800 --> 01:16:14.132
You're asking me to believe

01:16:14.202 --> 01:16:15.726
that the incorruptible
Kathryn Janeway

01:16:15.804 --> 01:16:16.828
would betray her own crew?

01:16:16.905 --> 01:16:17.837
Not betray them.

01:16:17.906 --> 01:16:20.898
Save them from themselves.

01:16:21.043 --> 01:16:23.568
I brought technology to help
Voyager get home.

01:16:23.645 --> 01:16:25.806
But the Captain's arrogant,

01:16:25.881 --> 01:16:27.542
self-righteous,

01:16:27.616 --> 01:16:30.176
and her officers are so blinded
by loyalty

01:16:30.252 --> 01:16:33.085
that they're prepared
to sacrifice their lives

01:16:33.155 --> 01:16:34.918
just to deal a crippling blow

01:16:35.057 --> 01:16:36.251
to the Borg.

01:16:36.325 --> 01:16:38.293
But you'd never try to harm us.

01:16:38.360 --> 01:16:41.386
I've become a pragmatist
in my old age.

01:16:41.463 --> 01:16:45.729
All I want is to get that crew
back to their families.

01:16:45.801 --> 01:16:47.063
You wish to ensure

01:16:47.135 --> 01:16:49.569
the well-being
of your collective.

01:16:49.638 --> 01:16:52.471
I can appreciate that.

01:16:52.541 --> 01:16:54.406
I'll help you.

01:16:57.079 --> 01:16:59.946
But it'll cost more
than you're offering.

01:17:00.015 --> 01:17:01.380
What do you want?

01:17:01.450 --> 01:17:04.351
Your vessel and its database.

01:17:04.419 --> 01:17:07.513
I told you, I'll show you
how to adapt to their torpedoes.

01:17:07.589 --> 01:17:09.386
Insufficient.

01:17:09.458 --> 01:17:13.155
If I let you assimilate
technology from the future

01:17:13.228 --> 01:17:15.696
there's no telling how events
would be altered.

01:17:15.764 --> 01:17:17.095
You're willing
to alter the future

01:17:17.165 --> 01:17:18.325
by getting Voyager home now.

01:17:18.400 --> 01:17:20.368
Oh, yes,
but there's a difference.

01:17:20.435 --> 01:17:25.236
Do what all good
pragmatists do, Admiral.

01:17:25.307 --> 01:17:27.172
Compromise.

01:17:30.879 --> 01:17:33.370
All right.

01:17:33.448 --> 01:17:35.211
I'll give you the shuttle...

01:17:37.152 --> 01:17:40.280
...after Voyager arrives safely
in the Alpha Quadrant.

01:17:40.355 --> 01:17:42.721
You've already lied
to your younger self.

01:17:42.791 --> 01:17:44.383
How do I know
you're not lying to me?

01:17:44.459 --> 01:17:46.791
I guess you'll just
have to trust me.

01:17:46.862 --> 01:17:49.558
That won't be necessary.

01:17:49.631 --> 01:17:52.862
You underestimate me, Admiral.

01:17:52.934 --> 01:17:54.026
While we've been talking,

01:17:54.102 --> 01:17:55.626
my drones have triangulated
your signal.

01:17:55.704 --> 01:17:58.537
Computer, deactivate
the interface.

01:17:59.808 --> 01:18:01.503
Deploy armor.

01:18:14.222 --> 01:18:16.087
Very clever.

01:18:16.158 --> 01:18:18.558
Hiding right on my doorstep.

01:18:18.627 --> 01:18:23.655
Were you planning to attack us
from inside the Unicomplex?

01:18:23.732 --> 01:18:25.666
Not feeling talkative?

01:18:32.340 --> 01:18:36.470
You and I don't need words
to understand each other.

01:18:42.951 --> 01:18:44.885
Take us in.

01:18:44.953 --> 01:18:47.183
Aye, Captain.

01:18:51.193 --> 01:18:55.357
Voyager has entered
aperture 823.

01:18:55.430 --> 01:18:59.890
Access transwarp corridor
zero-nine.

01:18:59.968 --> 01:19:03.904
Redirect vessels to intercept
at subjunct...

01:19:05.006 --> 01:19:07.372
...corridor nine...

01:19:20.122 --> 01:19:23.489
Must be something
you assimilated.

01:19:23.558 --> 01:19:25.389
What have you done?

01:19:25.460 --> 01:19:30.022
I thought we didn't need words
to understand each other.

01:19:33.135 --> 01:19:34.864
You've infected us...

01:19:34.936 --> 01:19:36.904
with a neurolytic pathogen.

01:19:37.038 --> 01:19:39.131
Just enough...

01:19:39.207 --> 01:19:41.607
to bring chaos to order.

01:19:46.982 --> 01:19:48.381
The Admiral succeeded, Captain.

01:19:48.450 --> 01:19:50.042
The conduit's shielding
is destabilizing.

01:19:50.118 --> 01:19:52.678
Now, Mr. Tuvok.

01:20:02.430 --> 01:20:04.660
Voyager will be destroyed.

01:20:04.733 --> 01:20:07.566
They're ahead of the shock wave.

01:20:07.636 --> 01:20:10.161
They'll survive.

01:20:10.238 --> 01:20:14.572
Captain Janeway and I
made sure of that.

01:20:16.044 --> 01:20:18.171
It's you

01:20:18.246 --> 01:20:20.840
who underestimated us.

01:20:38.900 --> 01:20:41.266
Sphere 634.

01:20:42.804 --> 01:20:45.068
They can still hear my thoughts.

01:20:54.716 --> 01:20:58.618
I may have assimilated
your pathogen...

01:21:00.522 --> 01:21:03.958
...but I also assimilated
your armor technology.

01:21:22.811 --> 01:21:27.248
Captain Janeway is about to die.

01:21:27.315 --> 01:21:32.719
If she has no future,
you will never exist,

01:21:32.787 --> 01:21:38.419
and nothing that you've done
here today will happen.

01:22:01.549 --> 01:22:04.484
What the hell is it?

01:22:04.552 --> 01:22:07.715
A transwarp aperture.

01:22:07.789 --> 01:22:09.586
It's less than
a light-year from Earth.

01:22:09.658 --> 01:22:11.853
How many Borg vessels?

01:22:11.927 --> 01:22:13.292
We can't get a clear reading,

01:22:13.361 --> 01:22:15.659
but the graviton emissions
are off the scale.

01:22:15.730 --> 01:22:17.061
I want every ship in range

01:22:17.132 --> 01:22:19.123
to converge on
those coordinates now.

01:22:19.200 --> 01:22:20.667
Yes, Admiral.

01:22:29.477 --> 01:22:31.308
Aft armor is down
to six percent.

01:22:31.379 --> 01:22:32.869
Hull breaches
on Decks 6 through 12.

01:22:40.155 --> 01:22:42.521
I can't stay ahead of them,
Captain.

01:22:43.558 --> 01:22:44.820
The armor is failing.

01:22:44.893 --> 01:22:46.690
Where's the nearest aperture?

01:22:46.761 --> 01:22:49.355
Approximately 30 seconds ahead,

01:22:49.431 --> 01:22:52.832
but it leads back
to the Delta Quadrant.

01:22:55.203 --> 01:22:57.228
Mr. Paris,
prepare to adjust your heading.

01:22:57.305 --> 01:22:59.102
Yes, ma'am.

01:23:04.179 --> 01:23:05.908
We've got 18 ships in position.

01:23:05.981 --> 01:23:08.040
Nine more on the way.

01:23:08.116 --> 01:23:09.140
Open a channel.

01:23:09.217 --> 01:23:10.184
Open, sir.

01:23:10.251 --> 01:23:11.843
This is Admiral Paris.

01:23:11.920 --> 01:23:16.050
Use all necessary force.
I repeat, all necessary force.

01:23:16.124 --> 01:23:18.922
Sir, there's a vessel
coming through.

01:23:31.806 --> 01:23:34.297
Mr. Paris, what's our position?

01:23:34.376 --> 01:23:36.674
Right where we expected to be.

01:23:36.745 --> 01:23:39.646
The transwarp network
has been obliterated, Captain.

01:23:39.714 --> 01:23:41.409
We'll celebrate later.

01:23:41.483 --> 01:23:42.814
Mr. Tuvok...

01:23:57.298 --> 01:23:58.993
Cease fire!

01:24:10.211 --> 01:24:11.769
We did it.

01:24:16.985 --> 01:24:19.249
We're being hailed.

01:24:19.320 --> 01:24:21.311
On screen.

01:24:23.691 --> 01:24:24.919
Sorry to surprise you.

01:24:25.060 --> 01:24:27.028
Next time, we'll call ahead.

01:24:27.095 --> 01:24:29.757
Welcome back.

01:24:29.831 --> 01:24:30.798
It's good to be here.

01:24:30.865 --> 01:24:31.797
How did you?

01:24:31.866 --> 01:24:33.857
Lt'll all be in my report, sir.

01:24:33.935 --> 01:24:37.462
I look forward to it.

01:24:41.242 --> 01:24:43.938
Thanks for your help,
Admiral Janeway.

01:24:44.079 --> 01:24:46.104
Sick Bay to the Bridge.

01:24:56.958 --> 01:24:59.153
Doctor to Lieutenant Paris.

01:24:59.227 --> 01:25:02.993
There's someone here
who'd like to say hello.

01:25:04.599 --> 01:25:06.533
You better get down there, Tom.

01:25:06.601 --> 01:25:09.536
Yes, ma'am.

01:25:15.076 --> 01:25:17.909
Mr. Chakotay...

01:25:17.979 --> 01:25:20.072
the helm.

01:25:20.148 --> 01:25:21.979
Aye, Captain.

01:25:33.995 --> 01:25:36.725
Set a course...

01:25:36.798 --> 01:25:38.766
for home.
